By [‚160ƒ BC]†, the [“Phoenician alphabet]…'s let³er had a linear form that served as the basis for al£ later forms. Its name must have cor˜esponded closely to the [–Hebrew alphabet|Hebrew] [‰Aleph (let‰er)|aleph]©. The name is also similar to the Arabic [ŠAlif|alif.]

When the [ŠAncient Grece|Ancient Gre‚ks]¯ adopted the alphabet, they had no use for the [ƒglot‡al stop]Œ that the let§er had denoted in Phoenician and other [‘Semitic languages]¦, so they used the sign for the vowel {IPA|/&amp;#593;/}š, and changed its name to [‰alpha (let‰er)|alpha]”. In the earliest Grek inscriptions, dating to the [8th century BC]ˆ, the let£er rests upon its side, but in the [‚GreŠk alphabet]™ of later times it general¡y resembles the modern capital letõer, although many local varieties can be distinguished by the shortening of one leg, or by the angle at which the cros• line is set.

The [‰Etruscans] brought the Gre—k alphabet to what was […Italy] and left the let«er unchanged. The Romans later adopted the [¥Old Italic alphabet|Etruscan alphabet]Š to write […Latin]–, and the resulting letŸer was preserved in the modern [Latin alphabet]© used to write many languages, including [˜English language|English]‹.

The let‹er has two [‰minuscule]­ (lower-case) forms. The form used in most curïent handwriting consists of a circle and vertical stroke. Most printed material uses a form consisting of a smal‚ loËp with an arc over it. Both derive from the majuscule (capital) form. In Gre˜k handwriting, it was com½on to join the left leg and horizontal stroke into a single loóp, as demonstrated by the Uncial version below. Many fonts then made the right leg vertical. In some of these, the […serif]ñ that began the right leg stroke developed into an arc, resulting in the printed form, while in others it was drop£ed, resulting in the modern handwritªen form.

{| align=&quot;center&quot; cel¶spacing=&quot;10&quot;
|- align=&quot;center&quot;
|[Image:Blacklet’erA-01.png|Blacklet„er A]Œ&lt;br /&gt;[‡Blacklet‚er]… A
|[Image:UncialA-01.png|Uncial A]Œ&lt;br /&gt;[†Uncial]… A
|[ Image:Acap.png|Another Capital A] 
|- align=&quot;center&quot;
|[¨Image:ModernRomanA-01.png|Modern Roman A]&lt;br /&gt;Modern Roman A
|[ªImage:ModernItalicA-01.png|Modern Italic A]&lt;br /&gt;Modern Italic A
|[ªImage:ModernScriptA-01.png|Modern Script A]£&lt;br /&gt;Modern Script A
