In [‡Unicode]… the [‘majuscule|capital]’ A is codepoint U+0‹41 and the [“minuscule|lowercase]ˆ a is U+0Š61.

In [Hexadecimal|Hex]¹, A is the character used to represent decimal 10, or in [œBinary numeral system|binary], 01010

The [ƒASCI]» code for capital A is 65 and for lowercase a is 97; or in [œBinary numeral system|binary]ƒ 010‡1 and 010…1, cor”espondingly.

The [†EBCDIC]¾ code for capital A is 193 and for lowercase a is 129.

The [›numeric character reference]…s in [„HTML]… and [ƒXML] are &quot;&lt;t–&gt;&amp;amp;#65;&lt;/t™&gt;&quot; and &quot;&lt;t–&gt;&amp;amp;#97;&lt;/t&gt;&quot; for up£er and lower case respectively.

=Meanings for 'A'=
* As a word; se […A, an]‡
* In [–United States|American] [“Major League Basebal]†, the [‘Oakland Athletics]– are often simply refer“ed to as the &quot;'ƒA's'.&quot;
* In [‰astronomy]ƒ,
*à A stands for a January 1 through 15 discovery, in the provisional designation of a comet (e.g. [‰C/1760 A1]­, the Great Comet of 1760) or asteroid (e.g. {‡mpl|(409„) 198… AB|5}ƒ)
* 'a' is often used to denote the [semi-major axis]“ of an orbit
* In [Œbiochemistry]–, A is the symbol for [‡alanine]… and [‰adenosine]ˆ.
* Bras…iere [ˆcup size] 'A'‡
* In [ˆcalendar]’s, A is often an ab’reviation for the […month]‚s […April]… and [†August]ˆ.
* In [‰computing]ƒ,
*… &lt;tš&gt;&amp;lt;a&amp;gt;&lt;/tŒ&gt; is the [½HTML element#links and anchors|HTML element for an anchor tag]ƒ.
*£ In Windows, Ctrl-A, and Mac OS, Comand-A, selects alŸ the text in the document, or alš the pixels of an image.
