*š A:\ is the conventional ad‚res‘ of the first flopy disk drive in [„CP/M]‡-based [operating system]Šs such as [ƒDOS]ƒ.
*Ã A is a security division (&quot;Verified Protection&quot;) in the […TCSEC]ˆ.
* In [‰education]„, a [—Grade (education)|grade]„ of 'A'‡ typicalÛy represents the highest score that students can achieve. This is sometimes coupled with a [„plus]/[…minus] sign, as in '‚A+'„ or '‚A-'•, or a number, as in '‚A1'‰. It is oc†asionalšy a grade one level below '‚A*'¨ (pronounced &quot;A Star&quot;).
