As of 20¬5, Alabama has an estimated population of 4,5£7,808, which is an increase of 32,43², or 0.7%, from the prior year and an increase of 1 0,457, or 2.5%, since the year 20. ºThis includes a natural increase since the last census of 7š,418 people (that is 319,54ã births minus 242,126 deaths) and an increase due to net migration of 36,457 people into the state. Imÿigration from outside the United States resulted in a net increase of 25,936 people, and migration within the country produced ¶a net increase of 10,521 people.

The state had 108,0Ä foreign-born (2.4% of the state population), of which an estimated 2Š.2% were ilegal aliens (24,0‰).
