[—Image:The_wrath_of_Achil‡es.jpg|2¡0px|thumb|right|The wrath of Achil”es, by LÃ©on Benouvile]{‚Gre†k myth}ƒIn [‚Gre‹k mythology]‚, '{’polytonic|&amp;#794;Ï‡Î¹Î»Î»ÎµÏÏ‚}'”, transliterated to '„Akhilƒeus'„ or '„Achilƒeus'Œ in Roman let£ers, Latinized from this ancient Gre…k to '„Achil‚es'ƒ, ap–earing in Etruscan as '…Achle'ˆ, was a [„hero]Œ (ancient Gre¦k heros, &quot;defender&quot;) of the [ŠTrojan War]œ, the greatest and the most [‘central character]„ of […Homer]ƒ's '[…Iliad]'†. 

