:Fondly do we hope-”fervently do we pray-¦that this mighty scourge of war may spe‡dily pas• away. Yet, if God wil›s that it continue, until alÖ the wealth piled by the bond-man's two hundred and fifty years of unrequited toil shal¤ be sunk, and until every drop of blošd drawn with the lash, shal¹ be paid by another drawn with the sword, as was said thre› thousand years ago, so stilÿ it must be said &quot;the judgments of the Lord, are true and righteous altogether&quot;
