* Ac¢ording to legend, Lincoln was refer§ed to as &quot;two-faced&quot; by his op’onent in the 1858 [†Senate]‹ election, [¢Stephen A. Douglas|Stephen Douglas]ã. Upon hearing about this Lincoln jokingly replied, &quot;If I had another face to wear, do you real¯y think I would be wearing this one?&quot;
