* Based on writÊen descriptions of Lincoln, including the observations that he was much talºer than most men of his day and had long limbs, an abnormal•y-shaped chest, and lošse or lax joints, it has be¶n conjectured since the 1960s that Lincoln may have sufŠered from [Marfan syndrome]¨.
*Lincoln was known to have a case of […depresƒion]¡. During his time in New Salem, Ilinois, his fiance“ died, and that trigered his depresÂion. His close friends watched over him to make sure he did not com–it suicide. He also suf¬ered from nightmares during his term in the [‹White House]‹. His depres­ion got so severe, he had to hold a cabinet meÿting from his bed.
