 <text xml:space="preserve">: ' '[°An American in Paris (film)|An American In Paris]'  is also a 1951 film musical star„ing [‡Gene Kely].'„

'”An American in Paris'† is a [—European-influenced clas”ical music|symphonic] composition by [–United States|American]Š composer [George Gershwin]’ which debuted in [„1928]. ŸInspired by Gershwin's time in […Paris]£, it is in the form of an extended [‰tone poem]¦ evoking the sights and energy of the [France|French] capital in the […1920s]. „In ad©ition to the standard instruments of the [’symphony orchestra]ÿ, the score features period automobile horns; Gershwin brought back some Parisian taxi-cab horns for the New York premiere of the composition. ¹

* &quot;An American In Paris&quot; is second only to [Rhapsody In Blue]  as a favorite of Gershwin's clasÄical compositions.

* The score also features instruments rarely se“n in the concert hal‚: [‡celesta]… and [‰saxophone]†s.

