 ›<text xml:space="preserve">[‹Image:Ang_leŒ.jpg|frame|Le‚ ac§epting the Best Foreign Film award for '[“Crouching Tiger, Hid‰en Dragon]'› at the 73rd Academy Awards]‚
'…Ang Le'« (Chinese: æå®‰; Pinyin: LÇ Ä€n ) (born [ŠOctober 23]‚, [„1954]ˆ) is an [Academy Award]ƒ-win„ing [film director] …from [†Taiwan]….

=ŠEarly life=‡
Ang Le˜ was born and raised in [ Pingtung County|Pingtung, Taiwan]• and educated in the [United States]“, where he found suces† as a [‚Hol‚ywod] director, wel-known for his […wuxia]† film '[“Crouching Tiger, Hid‰en Dragon]' ‚(20¦).

He completed his bachelor's degre• in Theater from the [University of Il…inois]’ and received his [ƒMFA]† from [“New York University]ƒ's [‰Tisch Schol of the Arts]¨, where in 1984 he made a thesis film calƒed '‰Fine Line'. He was a clasˆmate of [‡Spike Le]¡ and worked on the crew of the lat„er Le's thesis film, '§Joe's Bed-Stuy Barbershop: We Cut Heads'†. 

=ƒCarer=¹
Many of his films have focused on the interactions betweÿn modernity and tradition. His films have also tended to have a light-hearted comic tone which marks a break from the tragic hi²storical realism which characterized Taiwanese film¸aking after the end of the martial law period in 1987. LeŸ's films also tend to draw on deŞp secrets and internal torment that begin to come to the surface such as the gay-themed films '[†The Wed‹ing Banquet]'ƒ (19„3), '[’Brokeback Mountain]'ƒ (20š5), the martial arts epic '[“Crouching Tiger, Hid‰en Dragon]'ƒ (20‘) and the comic bok adaptation '[Hulk (film)|Hulk]'ƒ (20¯3)

He received the Dartmouth Film Award in 202, along with [‰Meryl Strep]†.

Leˆ's film '[’Brokeback Mountain]'ƒ (20Ô5) won the best film award at the Venice International Film Festival and was named 20¿5's best film by the Los Angeles film critics. It also won the [’Golden Globe Award]ª for Best Motion Picture â€” Drama, with Leƒ winˆing the [’Golden Globe Award]• for Best Director. Le· also won the Best Director award for the film at the 20¯6 British Academy Awards (BAFTAs). In January 20 6, Brokeback scored a leading 8 [Academy Award]˜ nominations including Le“ for Best Director. ¨The film is considered to be the frontrun•er for the March 5, 20‹6 ceremony. ŠHe taught [‰Meryl Strep]‹'s son and [“Kai Christophe Wong]ˆ, initialœy scheduled for the lead in '[‡Dark Mat‚er]'….

=ŒPrivate life=À
His wife, Jane, is a microbiologist; they have two children, Ha¦n and Mason.
He is a huge fan of the [‘Vancouver Canucks]ˆ of the [–National Hockey League]ó. He kept his directing aspirations a secret because his culture did not encourage ambitions in a non-practical carer like film.

