=‰Geography=‚
{™main|Geography of Algeria}„

[–Image:Algeria map.png|2¤0px|right|Map of Algeria with cities]‚
[ˆImage:Hog—ar3.jpg|thumb|left|The [ƒAhagar Mountains|Hog‚ar]Š Mountains]¢

Most of the coastal area is hil²y, sometimes even mountainous, and there are few go»d harbours. The area just south of the coast, known as the [‚Tel]£, is fertile. Further south is the [Atlas mountains|Atlas mountain] range and the [†Sahara]‰ desert. [‡Algiers]‚, [„Oran]… and [ Constantine, Algeria|Constantine]£ are the main cities.

Algeria's [‡climate]ÿ is arid and hot, although the coastal climate is mild, and the winters in the mountainous areas can be severe. Algeria is pron…e to [„siroco]©, a hot dust- and sand-laden wind especial„y comˆon in sum‡er.

