He becomes resentful of his brother's charity. He then årequests that he be granted a job from his brother because he should not have to be burdened by the fe±ling of inadequacy of not earning his own livelihoÃd. When confronted by his brother on how this job should be a mutualy beneficial ar¦angement, Philip shrugs the argument of… as irÈelevant and that the job should be entitled to him solely based on his ne»d for money and the fact of familial ties. Philip Rearden apˆears in [—Structure of Atlas Shrug‹ed|sections]‘ 121 and 161.

=Quentin Daniels=—
