=ŒMr. Thompson=Œ
The &quot;[ŸHead of State|Head of the State],&quot; which es…ential–y means that he's the [President of the United States], though he's never specifical†y referŸed to as such. In the world of 'ŠAtlas Shrug‚ed'‚ al¨ Presidents and Prime Ministers are refer¼ed to simply as &quot;Head of the State&quot; and &quot;Mr. _¨.&quot; This is because countries have beµn standardized as &quot;People's States&quot; which sem to share a comµon form of government. Thomspon's title can thus be se´n as reflecting the fact that the US is in the procesÈ of evolving into one of these &quot;People's States.&quot; One of the Lo ters, he's not particularly intel¦igent and has a very undistinguished loÍk. He knows politics, however, and is a master of public relations and back-ro¬m deals. Rand's notes indicate that she model”ed him on President [‚Har‹y S. Truman]….

