=ŒGalt's Motor=¯
John Galt invented a new type of electrical ap™aratus described in the bo‡k as a […motor]. ³However, it does not operate like a motor in the com™on use of the word today: –it is capable of harnes—ing, transforming and ap°lying energy in many ways other than mechanical. œGalt's Motor was capable of [ˆRadio jam†ing|jamƒing]‚ al [radio receiver]½s on Earth, and completely destroying the contents of Galt's [bo‡by-trap]Ÿped laboratory without causing [‚colateral damage|col˜ateral structural damage]«.


Though Rand describes it as turning [“static electricity ] into useful [mechanical work]À, its operation is more reminiscent of modern speculation about [‘zero-point energy]Ì.

Dagny discovers a discarded prototype of the motor and it is superficialy described in [—Structure of Atlas ShrugŠed|section]“ Part 1, Chapter 9. ¯Galt shows Dagny the motor and describes it in [—Structure of Atlas ShrugŠed|section]™ Part 3, Chapter 1.


