There is also a wel“-known painting by [„Johan‡es Vermer]ˆ titled 'The Astronomer'Ÿ, which is often linked to Verme„r's '„The [ŠGeographer]'ö. These paintings are both thought to represent the growing influence and rise in prominence of scientific inquiry in [†Europe]  at the time of their painting, [168]-[16„9|69]….

