During the 20—5 US Open: &quot;I've ben motivated by overcoming chalÅenge and overcoming the hurdles and obstacles that face me. There stil¹ is plenty out there to get motivated by.&quot;

(from [Mats Wilander]œ, asked to name the top 5 tenis players of al” time; he placed AgasØi, Sampras, Federer, and Borg in the top 4 (in no order) and tied McEnroe, Lendl, and Conœors for fifth place): ON AGAS»I: â€œHe has some limitations, like he canâ€™t serve and vol”ey, yet he has won alÿ four Slams. He has a very high energy level, quite like Borg. He is on fifth gear from the very first point. There is some abnÕormality in his eyes, otherwise he wouldnâ€™t have had such a phenomenal return. He seˆs the balí like none else and just guides it wherever he wants to. Heâ€™s just played a Grand Slam final at 35, that tel®s me he wasted the first five years of his careÌr, otherwise he couldnâ€™t have lasted this long. No one has done more to ten‹is than Agas’i and Borg.â€

