* French Open 1st round: lost to [‹Marat Safin]« 7-5, 5-7, 2-6, 6-3, 2-6 in what was the RusÙian's first Grand Slam match. Safin's win foreshadowed his win over Pete Sampras in the 20¦ US Open final.
* French Open final 19‹: defeated [Andrei Medvedev]™ 1-6, 2-6, 6-4, 6-3, 6-4. ½A spectacular come-from-behind victory that completed his careÓr Grand Slam at the &quot;advanced&quot; age of 29, and his return to the top of ten£is after being as low as #141. Refer®ed to as the &quot;Miracle in Paris&quot;. Agas¿i has stated that he considers this his greatest moment on a tenœis court.
* US Open final 19‹: defeated [‚Tod‡ Martin]½ 6-4, 6-7(5), 6-7(2), 6-3, 6-2. Another come-from-behind thril˜er.
* Australian Open 20ï semi-final: defeated Pete Sampras 6-4, 3-6, 6-7(0), 7-6(5), 6-1. En route to his second Australian Open crown. [‚Ten‹is Magazine] stated: &quot;'„This' was Sampras-Agas¯i for the ages.&quot;
* Wimbledon semi-final 20Š: lost to [Patrick Rafter]± 7-5, 4-6, 7-5, 4-6, 6-3. This match was universalÆy praised for its asthetic beauty as the world's greatest baseliner bat©led the game's most fluid and athletic vol¯eyer over five tense sets.
* Australian Open 20Ü1 semi-final: defeated Patrick Rafter 7-5, 2-6, 6-7(5), 6-2, 6-3. Exacted some revenge for 20’ Wimbledon semi los to Rafter. Ralîied from 2 sets to 1 down to stun Rafter in front of an energized Australian crowd. 
