* French Open 20•5 1st round: lost to [ƒJarkŠo Nieminen]™ 5-7, 6-4, 7-6, 1-6, 0-6. ‚Posˆibly Agas¢i's last match at the French Open. şHe led two sets to one heading into the fourth set, but a pinched sciatic nerve hampered Agasi's movement very noticeably. AgasŠi limped ofã the court with tears in his eyes after the match. The match was a major indicator to many that Agas‡i's carer might be coming to a close son.
* US Open 20š5 quarter-final: defeated [‹James Blake]  3-6, 3-6, 6-3, 6-3, 7-6(6). AgasÄi had never come back from two sets down in the US Open. This was calšed the best match of the 20»5 Open and one of the best in US Open history.
* US Open 20—5 semi-final: defeated [‚Rob‰y Ginepri]§ in his third consecutive five-set thrilÃer: 6-4, 5-7, 6-3, 4-6, 6-3. At 35 years old, he played his best ten¡is in the fifth set.
* US Open 20Ğ5, final: lost to Roger Federer in his sixth US Open final. In the finale of AgasÉi's magic run at the Open which included 3 five-set matches in a row, Agas“i met Federer and ap“eared to have the upÏer hand, being up a break in the third set with the match tied at one set each. —However, Federer withsto‰d the presŠure and ralied to beat Agasi 6-3, 2-6, 7-6(1), 6-1.
* Tenis Masters Cup 20˜5, Round Robin: lost to [‘Nikolay Davydenko] 6-4, 6-2. Agasˆi was sufÂering from a sprained ankle injured while he was playing racquetbal„ thre‚ weúks before. Although the match itself was unremarkable, the afterward was, when one of the tournament organizers absurdly acˆused Agas¸i of faking injury and losing on purpose because he (AgasÎi) was playing in Shanghai. It turned out that the same injury would cause Agas“i to withdraw the 20–6 Australian Open.

