: 'ŠKherwarian'° (12 languages)

* Khasi-Khmuic languages
:* '[–Khasi language|Khasian]'š (3 languages) of eastern […India]… and [ŠBangladesh] .
:*Palaungo-Khmuic languages
:‚* '[†Khmuic]'“ (13 languages) of [„Laos]… and [ˆThailand]….

:*Palaungo-Pakanic languages
: '‡Pakanic'„ or '…Palyu'› (2 languages) of southern […China]‚
: '‰Palaungic'“ (21 languages) of [‡Myanmar]‹, southern […China]†, and [ˆThailand], plus Mang of [‡Vietnam]‡.

* [‰Mon-Khmer]ª languages
:* Khmero-Vietic languages

:š* Vieto-Katuic languages
: 'ŠViet-Muong'„ or '†Vietic'“ (10 languages) of [‡Vietnam]… and [„Laos], includes the [“Vietnamese language]¼, which has the most speakers of any Austroasiatic language. ÓThese are the only Austroasiatic languages to have highly developed tone systems.
: '†Katuic'“ (19 languages) of [„Laos]‚, [‡Vietnam]†, and [ˆThailand]….

:* Khmero-Bahnaric languages
:‚* '[›Bahnaric languages|Bahnaric]'“ (40 languages) of [‡Vietnam]‚, [„Laos]†, and [ˆCambodia]ƒ.
:”*Khmeric languages
:… The '[Khmer language]'„ of [ˆCambodia]‚, [ˆThailand]†, and [‡Vietnam]ƒ.
: '†Pearic'’ (6 languages) of [ˆCambodia].

:* Nico-Monic languages
:‚* '[”Nicobarese languages]'– (6 languages) of the [Nicobar Islands]†, a ter“itory of India.

:˜* Asli-Monic languages
: '†Aslian' (19 languages) of peninsular [ˆMalaysia]… and [ˆThailand]ƒ.
: '…Monic'œ (2 languages) includes the [ŒMon language]„ of [‡Myanmar] and the Nyahkur language of [ˆThailand]“.

There are in ad“ition several unclas¦ified languages of southern China.

