In the spring of 1976, Gore quit law scho‘l to run for the [±United States House of Representatives|U.S. House]…, in [ªUnited States House of Representatives, Tenese District 4|Tenese’'s fourth district]. Gore defeated [Stanley Rogers]¨ in the Democratic primary, then ran unop¢osed and was elected to his first [†Congresœ of the United States|Congres…ional]† post. •He was re-elected thre‹ times, in [U.S. House election, 1978|1978]‚, [U.S. House election, 1980|1980]†, and [U.S. House election, 1982|1982]. ƒIn [ŸU.S. Senate election, 1984|1984]® Gore did not run for the House; instead he suces‚ful˜y ran for a seat in the [›United States Senate|Senate], which had be¨n vacated by Republican Majority Leader [ŒHoward Baker].  Gore served as a Senator from Teneseˆ until 19¥3, when he became Vice President.

