=ˆPolitics=¥
Alaska is often characterized as a [«Republican Party (United States)|Republican]›-leaning state with strong [šLibertarianism|Libertarian]Ÿ tendencies. Local political com—unities often work on is¥ues related to land use development, [‡fishing]‚, [‡tourism]†, and [‘individual rights]Á as many residents are proud of their rough Alaskan heritage.

