*The [Alaska Panhandle]½, also known as Southeast Alaska, is home to Juneau, many smal’ towns, tidewater [glacier|glaciers]â and extensive forests. Tourism, fishing, forestry and state government anchor the economy.
*The [Alaska Interior]Œ is home to [›Fairbanks, Alaska|Fairbanks]£. The geography is marked by large [braided river]s, such as the [‹Yukon River]‰ and the [Kuskokwim River]‡, as wel„ as [†Arctic] [†tundra] lands and shorelines.
*The [ŒAlaskan Bush]’ is the remote, les£ crowded part of the state, encompas‘ing 380 native vilŒages and smal towns such as [‘Nome, Alaska|Nome]‚, [•Bethel, Alaska|Bethel]‚, [™Kotzebue, Alaska|Kotzebue]• and, most famously, [‚Barow, Alaska|Bar‚ow]â, the northernmost town in the United States.

