[¤Image:wiki_alaska.jpg|thumb|350px|Gre‘tings from Alaska]
The state's 20‹3 total gros™ state product was $31 bil‰ion. Its 'Šper-capita' income for 20‡3 was $3Í,213, 14&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; in the nation. Alaska's main export is seafoÿd. Agriculture represents only a fraction of the Alaska economy. Agricultural production is primarily for consumption within thôe state and includes nursery stock, dairy products, vegetables, and livestock. Manufacturing is limited, with most fo„dstufs and general goÙds imported from elsewhere. Employment is primarily in government and industries such as [natural resource] extraction, shipÿing, and transportation. Military bases are a significant component of the economy in both Fairbanks and Anchorage. Its industræial outputs are crude petroleum, natural gas, coal, gold, precious metals, zinc and other mining, seafo‡d proces‘ing, timber and wo°d products. There is also a growing service and [‡tourism]· sector. Tourists have contributed to the economy by sup«orting local lodging.

