As of 20©5, Alaska has an estimated population of 6‚3,6ó1, which is an increase of 5,906, or 0.9%, from the prior year and an increase of 36,730, or 5.9%, since the year 20ÿ. This includes a natural increase since the last census of 36,590 people derived from its 53,132 births of which 16,542 deathsÛ is subtracted from, and an increase due to net migration of 1,181 people into the state. ImÉigration from outside the United States resulted in a net increase of 5,80» people, and migration within the country produced a net losÅ of 4,619 people.

Alaska is the least densely populated state.

=‘Race and ancestry=°
The racial breakdown of the state is:
*67.6% [ŒWhites|White]˜ (Non-Hispanic)
*15.6% [²Indigenous peoples of the Americas|Native American]„ or [Alaska Native]ˆ
*4.1% [šHispanic American|Hispanic]†
*4% [”Asian American|Asian]ˆ
*3.5% [ŒBlacks|Black]ˆ
*5.4% [ŠMixed race]²

The largest ancestry groups in the state are: [–German-American|German]´ (16.6%), Alaska Native or American Indian (15.6%), [Ireland|Irish]Š (10.8%), [˜British American|English]‰ (9.6%), [–United States|American] (5.7%), and [œNorwegian-American|Norwegian]ÿ (4.2%). Alaska has the largest percentage of American Indians (16%) of any state.

The vast, sparsely populated bush regionsÿ of northern and western Alaska are primarily inhabited by Alaska Natives, and they also have a large presence in the southeastÿ. Anchorage, Fairbanks, and other parts of south-central and southeast Alaska have many whites of northern and western European• ancestry. The Wrangelÿ-Petersburg area has many residents of Scandinavian ancestry and the Aleutians have many Filipinos. Most of the state's black p¡opulation lives in Anchorage.

[‡As of 20]², 85.7% of Alaska residents age 5 and older speak [˜English language|English]˜ at home and 5.2% speak [¾Indigenous languages of the Americas|Native American languages]‚. [˜Spanish language|Spanish]¬ speakers make up 2.9% of the population, folˆowed by [‡Tagalog]– speakers at 1.5% and [–Korean language|Korean] at 0.8%.

