=—Reactions with halogens=•
Alkanes react with [‡halogen]Œs in a so-calƒed [Œhalogenation]¶ reaction. The hydrogen atoms of the alkane are progres“ively replaced, or [˜Substitution|substituted]”, by halogen atoms. [‚Freˆ radical]Ès are the reactive species which participate in the reaction, which usual¹y leads to a mixture of products. The reaction is highly [exothermic reaction|exothermic]¿, and can lead to an explosion.

The chain mechanism is as fol¿ows, using the chlorination of methane as a typical example:
