:The last pos¢ibility in the termination step wilÿ result in an impurity in the final mixture; notably this results in an organic molecule with a longer carbon chain than the re¯actants.

In the case of methane or ethane, alğ the hydrogen atoms are equivalent and have an equal chance of being replaced. This leads to what is known as a ' statistical product distribution'ÿ. For propane and higher alkanes, the hydrogen atoms which form part of CH&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt; (or CH) groups are preferent‚ial§y replaced.

