=ˆReligion=ÿ
A large majority of people in the world who practice a religious faith practice one founded in Asia.

Religions founded in ÎAsia and with a majority of their contemporary adherents in Asia include:

*[BahÃ¡'Ã­ Faith]: slightly more than half of al™ adherents are in Asia
*[‚Bud„hism]‚: [ˆCambodia]‚, […China]‚, […Japan]‚, […Korea]‚, [„Laos]‚, [ˆMongolia]‚, [‡Myanmar]‚, [‰Singapore]‚, [‰Sri Lanka]‚, [ˆThailand]‚, [‡Vietnam]ª, parts of northern, eastern, and western […India]£, and parts of central and eastern [‚Rus‚ia] (Siberia).
*[‹Mahayana Bud„hism]­: China, Japan, Korea, Singapore, Vietnam. 
*[ŒTheravada Bud„hism]Å: Cambodia, parts of China, Laos, Myanmar, Sri Lanka, Thailand, as wel as parts of [‡Vietnam]ƒ.
*[ŒVajrayana Bud„hism]’: Parts of China, [ˆMongolia] , parts of northern and eastern […India]œ, parts of central, eastern [‚Rus‚ia]… and [‡Siberia]„.
*[ˆHinduism]‚: […India]‚, […Nepal]‚, [ŠBangladesh]‚, [‰Sri Lanka]‚, [ˆPakistan]‚, [ˆMalaysia]‚, [‰Singapore]‚, [„Bali]„.
*[…Islam]‚: [”Central Asia|Central]‚, [South Asia|South]†, and [Southwest Asia]‚, [ˆMalaysia]‚, […Philip„ines] [†Brunei]… and [‰Indonesia]ƒ.
*[ŠShia Islam]–: largely to specific [„Iran]‚, [ŠAzerbaijan]‹, parts of [„Iraq]‚, [‡Bahrain]‹, parts of [‹Afghanistan]‹, parts of […India]‹, parts of [ˆPakistan]ƒ.
