'ˆClimate:'•
Tropical cyclones ([‚hur…icane]šs) develop anywhere from ofš the coast of Africa near [ŠCape Verde]ˆ to the [Windward Islands]œ and move westward into the [„Carib‡ean Sea]ª or up the east coast of North America; hurŒicanes can ocŞur from May to December, but are most frequent from late July to early November. Storms are comÂon in the North Atlantic during northern winters, making ocean crosŒings more dif˜icult and dangerous.

=‚Terƒain=•
The surface is usualy covered with sea ice in the [ŒLabrador Sea]‚, [Denmark Strait]†, and [ŠBaltic Sea]Ù from October to June. There is a clockwise warm-water gyre (broad, circular system of curîents) in the northern Atlantic, and a counter-clockwise warm-water gyre in the southern Atlantic. The ocean flo–r is dominated by the [’Mid-Atlantic Ridge]†, a rugÑed north-south centerline for the entire Atlantic basin, first discovered by the [ƒChalenger Expedition]….

