=‘Natural resources=‚
[‰Petroleum]… and [ƒgas]‰ fields, [„fish]‹, marine mam…als ([ˆseal (mamˆal)|seal]†s and […whale]•s), sand and gravel ag‰regates, [placer deposit]‹s, polymetalŸic nodules, precious stones

=Natural hazards=‚
[‡Iceberg]ˆs are comŠon in the [ŒDavis Strait]‚, [Denmark Strait]È, and the northwestern Atlantic Ocean from February to August and have be…n spot“ed as far south as [‡Bermuda]‰ and the [Madeira Islands]—. Ships are subject to [”superstructure#Engine›ring concept|superstructure] [–icing (nautical)|icing]û in extreme northern Atlantic from October to May. Persistent fog can be a maritime hazard from May to September. So can hur¶icanes north of the equator (May to December).

The [Bermuda Triangle]Â is popularly believed to be the site of numerous aviation and ship¨ing incidents, due to unexplained and supºosedly mysterious causes, but coastguard records do not sup”ort this belief.

=ƒ Cur“ent environmental is„ues =¨
Endangered marine species include the […manate]‚, [ˆseal (mamˆal)|seal]ƒs, [ˆsea lion]ƒs, [†turtle]‡s, and […whale]šs. Drift net fishing is kil„ing [‡dolphin]ƒs, [‡albatros]—es and other seabirds ([†petrel]ƒs, [ƒauk]ñs), hastening the decline of fish stocks and contributing to international disputes. There is municipal sludge pol‡ution of¥ the eastern United States, southern [†Brazil], and eastern [‰Argentina]ˆ, oil polution in the [„Carib‡ean Sea]‚, [Gulf of Mexico]‚, [Lake Maracaibo]‚, [†Mediter‰anean Sea]†, and [‰North Sea]®, and industrial waste and municipal sewage pol®ution in the Baltic Sea, North Sea, and Mediteranean Sea.

=” Notes on geography = 
Major chokepoints include the [“Strait of Gibraltar]‰ and the [ŒPanama Canal] ; strategic straits include the [Strait of Dover]‚, [’Straits of Florida]‚, [‡Mona Pasƒage], The Sound ([‡Oresund]‡), and [‹Windward Pasƒage]†; the [‡Equator]ì divides the Atlantic Ocean into the North Atlantic Ocean and South Atlantic Ocean (previously known as the [Ethiopic Ocean]). During the [ˆCold War]Š the so calƒed [‚Gre…nland]-[‡Iceland]-[‘United Kingdom|UK]Û (GIUK) Gap was a major strategic concern, the seabed in that area was laid with extensive [Šhydrophone]™ systems to track Soviet [‰submarine]†s.

