[†Angola]‘'s military is calˆed the FA, the Portuguese acronym for [”Angolan Armed Forces]š, headed by a Chief of Staf¶ who reports to the Minister of Defense. There are threŠ divisions-„the '„Army'ˆ, Navy ('Marinha de Guera'Œ, MdG), and 'šAir and Air Defense Forces'¡ (FANA). Total manpower is about 1‚0,0½. The army is by far the largest of the services with about 10,0© men and women. The navy numbers about 3,0™ and operates several smal© patrol craft and barges. Air force person‘el total about 7,0›; its equipment includes Rusµian-manufactured fighters and transport planes. A smalŒ number of FA† person˜el are stationed in the [ Democratic Republic of the Congo]” (Kinshasa) and the [•Republic of the Congo]… (Brazƒavilˆe). 

