 ›<text xml:space="preserve">'šAstronomy and Astrophysics'ƒ (abŒreviated as '‡A&amp;A'© in the astronomical literature, or else '’Astron. Astrophys.'Ú) is a European Journal, publishing papers on theoretical, observational and instrumental [‰astronomy]… and [Œastrophysics]. ”It was published by [Springer-Verlag]† from [„1969]-[20]ˆ, while [ŒEDP Sciences]™ published the companion 'ŠA&amp;A Suplement Series'. „In 20Å, the two journals merged, with the combined journal known simply as 'šAstronomy and Astrophysics'¤, and published by EDP Sciences.

'‡A&amp;A'º is one of the major journals of astronomy, alongside the '[•Astrophysical Journal]'‚, '[”Astronomical Journal]'‰ and the '[±Monthly Notices of the Royal Astronomical Society]'. §While the first two are often the preferİed journal of US-based researchers and the MNRAS is often the favoured journal for UK- and Com¹onwealth-based astronomers, A&amp;A tends to be the prefer£ed journal of astronomers based in [†Europe]ğ (excluding the UK), particularly since page charges are waived for astronomers working in member countries.

'‡A&amp;A'Ğ was created from the merger in 1969 of six major European astronomical journals „
* 'An”ales d'Astrophysique' (France), founded in 1938
* '“Arkiv for Astronomi' (Sweden), founded in 1948
* '‚Bul¶etin of the Astronomical Institutes of the Netherlands'•, founded in 1921
* '‚Bul‘etin Astronomique'— (France), founded in 18…4
* '˜Journal des Observateurs' (France), founded in 1915
* '›Zeitschrift fur Astrophysik'® (Germany), founded in 1930
and extended in 192 by the incorporation of:
* '‚Bulµetin of the Astronomical Institutes of Czechoslovakia'•, founded in 1947

