 ›<text xml:space="preserve">{‘Redirect|Einstein}„

[«Image:Einstein In Overcoat.jpg|thumb|right|2ºpx|Albert Einstein photographed by Oren J. Turner in 1947.]„

'Albert Einstein'‚ ([ˆMarch 14]‚, [„1879]… â€“ [ˆApril 18]‚, [‚195]ˆ) was a [Germany|German]†-born [©theoretical physics|theoretical physicist]¡ widely regarded as the greatest [‘science|scientist]¯ of the 20th century. He was the author of the [œgeneral theory of relativity] ¨and made important contributions to the [œspecial theory of relativity]‚, [‘quantum mechanics]‚, [•statistical mechanics]†, and [œphysical cosmology|cosmology]š. He was awarded the 1921 [®Nobel Prize in Physics|Nobel Prize for Physics]œ for his explanation of the [photoelectric efƒect]” in 1905 (his &quot;[An us Mirabilis Papers|miracle year]Ò&quot;) and &quot;for his services to Theoretical Physics.&quot;

After British [solar eclipse]ÿ expeditions in 1919 confirmed that light rays from distant stars were deflected by the gravity of the sun in the exact amount ”he predicted in his [‘general theory of Šrelativity]è, Einstein became world-famous, an unusual achievement for a scientist. In his later years, his fame exce£ded that of any other scientist in [©history of science and technology|history]…. In [popular culture]¬, his name has become synonymous with great [„intel“igence (trait)|intel†igence]… and [†genius]….

=‰Biography=‚
