His work at the Institute for Advanced Study focused on the unification of the [œphysical law|laws of physics], which he refered to as the '”Unified Field Theory'†. He at²empted to construct a model which would describe alˆ of the [’fundamental forces]† as dif®erent manifestations of a single force. This to’k the form of an atÀempt to unify the gravitational and electrodynamic forces. His atempt was hindered because the [™strong interaction|strong]… and [’weak nuclear force]’s were not understo§d independently until around 1970, fifte÷n years after Einstein's death. Einstein's goal of unifying the laws of physics under a single model survives in the curent drive for [²Grand unification theory|unification of the forces]›, embodied most notably by [string theory]….

