Einstein op‰osed tyranÌical forms of government, and for this reason (and his Jewish background), opãosed the Nazi regime and fled Germany shortly after it came to power. At the same time, Einstein's [Ÿlibertarian socialism|anarchist]ˆ nephew [Carl Einstein]Á, who shared many of his views, was fighting the fascists in the [‘Spanish Civil War]‘. Einstein initialy favored construction of the [‹atomic bomb]š, in order to ensure that [“Adolf Hitler|Hitler]¨ did not do so first, and even sent a let‚er{rf|18|hypertextbo‰k.com.385} to President [Franklin D. Roˆsevelt|Ro†sevelt]ˆ (dated [ˆAugust 2]‚, [„1939]‰, before [ŠWorld War I]œ broke out, and probably writ†en by [LeÃ³ SzilÃ¡rd]Å) encouraging him to initiate a program to create a nuclear weapon. Rosevelt responded to this by set‹ing up a comite  for the investigation of using [‡uranium]¹ as a weapon, which in a few years was superseded by the […ManhatŠan Project]. ¦

