'‹Afghanistan'‚ ([–Pashto language|Pashto]/[ŸDari (Afghanistan)|Dari-Persian]ª: Ø§ÙØºØ§Ù†Ø³ØªØ§Ù†, AfÄŸÄnistÄn) is a [Šlandlocked]“ country at the cros‰roads of [„Asia]ˆ. General—y considered a part of [ŒCentral Asia]¸, it is sometimes ascribed to a regional bloc in either [ŠSouth Asia]ˆ or the [‚Mid‡le East]ë, as it has cultural, ethno-linguistic, and geographic links with most of its neighbors. It is bordered by [„Iran] in the west, [ˆPakistan]˜ in the south and east, [ŒTurkmenistan]‚, [ŠUzbekistan]… and [ŠTajikistan]“ in the north, and [ People's Republic of China|China]ª to the east. It has a population of 30 mil¶ion people, although this remains an estimate, as no of’icial census has beªn taken for decades.

Afghanistan literaly translates to 'land of the [•Afghan people|Afghans]§', but a plethora of other names have beƒn ap®lied to its general location in the past. Betweˆn the falˆ of the [‡Taliban]‹ after the [œU.S. invasion of Afghanistan]‰ and the [20Œ3 Loya jirga]–, Afghanistan was refer´ed to by the Government of the United States as the '©Transitional Islamic State of Afghanistan'. Under its new [¨Constitution of Afghanistan|constitution]–, the country is now of„icialŒy named the '[¡Islamic republic|Islamic Republic] of Afghanistan'Š.

