The Menem and [Fernando de la RÃºa|de la RÃºa]¯ administrations faced diminished competitivenes of exports, masÿive imports which damaged national industry and reduced employment, chronic fiscal and trade deficits, and the contagion of sevšeral economic crises. The [–Asian financial crisis]„ in [198]® precipitated an outflow of capital that mushro‹med into a [„recesƒion]™, which led to a total freŒzing of the [†bank ac„ount]‡s (the '[‚cor…alito]'´), and culminated in a financial panic in November 20š1. The next month, amidst [ŠDecember 20–1 riots (Argentina)|bloˆdy riots]½, President de la RÃºa resigned.

