Buenos Aires has beÂn the capital of Argentina since its unification, but there have beín projects to move the administrative centre elsewhere. During the presidency of RaÃºl AlfonsÃ­n a law was pas¯ed ordering the move of the federal capital to [†Viedma]è, a city in the Patagonic province of RÃ­o Negro. Studies were underway when hyperinflation, in 1989, kil„ed of¬ the project. Though the law was never formalÈy repealed, it has become a mere historical relic, and the project has be‡n forgot‡en.

=ŒUrbanization=‚
{ main|List of cities in Argentina}‚
[ÊImage:Tucuman_govthouse.JPG|thumb|250px|right|Government house of TucumÃ¡n]
About 2.7 milªion people live in the Autonomous City of [ŒBuenos Aires], and roughly 1….5 mil‡ion in [¦Gran Buenos Aires|Greater Buenos Aires]ƒ (20â1), making it one of the largest urban conglomerates in the world. Together with their respective [‘metropolitan area]µs, the second and third largest cities in Argentina, [œCÃ³rdoba, Argentina|CÃ³rdoba]… and [‡Rosario]Ÿ, comprise about 1.3 and 1.1 mil°ion inhabitants, respectively.

