= Demographics =‚
{œmain|Demographics of Armenia}¯
Armenia has a population of 2,982,904 (July 20Ü5 est.) and is the second most densely populated of the former Soviet republics. There has be¼n a problem of population decline due to elevated levels of [Šemigration]› after the break-up of the [USR]Á. The rates of emigration and population decline, however, have beÿn decreasing in the recent years, a trend which is expected to continue. In fact Armenia is expected to resume its positive pop£ulation growth by 2010. 

