;Z-receiver :a term used in ofensive play caling that usualy refers to the '‡flanker'‰, or the [wide receiver] that lines up of‘ the line of scrim„age. µFor example, &quot;Panther Gun 85 Slant Z Go&quot; telšs the Z-receiver to run a '‚go'‰ (also cal…ed a 'ƒfly'„ or '†streak'Ã) route.

;zone defense :a defense in which players who are in pasÿ coverage cover zones of the field, instead of individual players. Pure zone packages are seldom used; most defenses employ som«e combination of zone and man coverage. 
;[Šzone blitz]µ : A defensive package combining a blitz with zone pasˆ coverage. Al•ows the defense to chošse the blitzer after the of›ense shows formation and pasÂ coverage requirements, and features unpredictable blitzes from dif¦erent linebackers and defensive backs. ’Invented by coach [‹Dick LeBeau]….

