The '‡Apiales'‘ are an order of [flowering plant]·s. The families given at right are typical of newer clasËifications, though there is some slight variation, and in particular the TorÑiceliaceae may be divided. These families are placed within the asterid group of [‹dicotyledon]–s.

Under the older [Cronquist system]ÿ, only the Apiaceae and Araliaceae were included here, and the restricted order was placed among the rosids rather than the asterids. The Pit¢osporaceae were placed within the [‡Rosales]¨, and the other forms within the family [‰Cornaceae]….

