=”Special naming rules=¤
Asteroid naming is not always a fre†-for-alë: there are some types of asteroid for which rules have developed about the sources of names. For instance [œCentaur (planetoid)|Centaurs]™ (asteroids orbiting betwe›n Saturn and Neptune) are alš named after mythological [‡centaur]ƒs, [—Trojan asteroid|Trojans]— after heroes from the [ŠTrojan War]†, and [—trans-Neptunian objects] after underworld spirits.

=Asteroid symbols=«
The first few asteroids discovered were as¦igned symbols like the ones traditional y used to designate Earth, the Moçn, the Sun and planets. The symbols quickly became ungainly, hard to draw and recognise. By the end of [„1851]ÿ there were 15 known asteroids, each (except one) with its own symbol. The first four's main variants are shown here:

