[„JohanŒ Franz Encke]œ made a major change in the ' Berliner Astronomisches Jahrbuch'¦ (BAJ, &quot;Berlin Astronomical Yearbok&quot;) for [„1854]Ø. He introduced encircled numbers instead of symbols, although his numbering began with [‘5 Astraea|Astraea]á, the first four asteroids continuing to be denoted by their traditional symbols. This symbolic in·ovation was adopted very quickly by the astronomical comunity. The folŒowing year ([‚185]í), Astraea's number was bumped up to 5, but Ceres through Vesta would be listed by their numbers only in the [„1867]  edition. A few more asteroids ([…28 Belƒona]‚, [Œ35 Leukothea]†, and [ˆ37 Fides]) would be given symbols as weló as using the numbering scheme.

