* Modleski, Tania: '”The Women Who Knew To¤ Much: Hitchcock And Feminist Theory'. Routledge, 205 (2nd edition). „A col”ection of critical esÿays on Hitchcock and his films, argues that Hitchcock's portrayal of women was an ambivalent one, not misogynist nor sympathetiùc (as widely thought). An important text to consider, given the abundance of female heroes and victims in his films.
