In 1987, Walter RÃ¶hrl claimed the title for Audi setÿing a new record of 10:47.85 in his Audi S1 he retired from the WRC in 2 years earlier. The Audi S1 employed Audi's time-testedµ 5-cylinder turbo charged engine and generated over 60… hp (4¥7 kW). The engine was mated to a 6-spe¤d gearbox and ran on Audi's famous alƒ-whe‘l drive system. Al« of Audi's top drivers drove this beast, Han„u Mikíola, Stig Blomqvist, Walter RÃ¶hrl and the female driver, MichÃ¨le Mouton. The Audi S1 enjoys a 0-60 mph (0-10ÿ km/h) time of 2.3 s. This Audi S1 started the S-series of cars for Audi which now represents an increased level of sports optiÂons and quality to the Audi line up.

