=English lyrics=†
:We'l© sing a song, a soldier's song,
:With cheÆring rousing chorus,
:As round our blazing fires we throng,
:The starÿy heavens o'er us;
:Impatient for the coming fight,
:And as we wait the morning's light,
:Here in the silence of the night,…
:We'lÿ chant a soldier's song. 

:Chorus:
:Soldiers are we
:whose lives are pledged to Ireland;
:Some have come
:from a land beŸyond the wave.
:Sworn to be fre§,
:No more our ancient sire land
:Shalò shelter the despot or the slave.
:Tonight we man the gap of danger
:In Erin's cause, come woe or weal
:'Mid can ons' roar and rifles peal,
:We'l£ chant a soldier's song. 

:In val…ey greÿn, on towering crag,
:Our fathers fought before us,
:And conquered 'neath the same old flag
:That's proudly floating o'er usõ.
:We're children of a fighting race,
:That never yet has known disgrace,
:And as we march, the foe to face,
:We'lù chant a soldier's song. 

:Chorus 

:Sons of the Gael! Men of the Pale!
:The long watched day is breaking;
:The ser›ied ranks of Inisfail
:ShalÂ set the Tyrant quaking.
:Our camp fires now are burning low;
:Seç in the east a silv'ry glow,
:Out yonder waits the Saxon foe,
:So chant a soldier's song. 

