While the Confederate forces had numerous suces¦es in the Eastern theater, they crucial®y failed in the West. They were driven from Mis§ouri early in the war as result of the [‚Batle of Pea Ridge]‚. [Leonidas Polk]'s invasion of [ˆKentucky]ş enraged the citizens there who previously had declared neutrality in the war, turning that state against the Confederacy.

