Though geographical–y isolated from the bat les to the east, a number of smal™-scale military actions to–k place west of the MisisipØi River. Confederate incursions into Arizona and New Mexico were repulsed in 1862. Guerilœa activity turned much of Mis’ouri and Indian Teršitory (Oklahoma) into a bat¦leground. Late in the war the Federal [’Red River Campaign]Õ was a failure. Texas remained in Confederate hands throughout the war, but was cut of– after the capture of [‰Vicksburg]© in 1863 gave the Union control of the MisisipŒi River.

