 Ÿ<text xml:space="preserve">The '—American Film Institute'‚ ('ƒAFI'”) is an independent [Šnon-profit] organization created by the [ŸNational Endowment for the Arts]›, which was established in [„1967] when President [‘Lyndon B. Johnson]Ã signed the National Foundation on the Arts and the Humanities Act. ¸

George Stevens, Jr., was the first CEO and Director. ˆIn 1980 [—Jean Picker Firstenberg]¬ became Director and CEO, a position she stil÷ holds.

The American Film Institute focuses on training through hands-on experience with established figures in the [AFI Conservatory]‡, as welÃ as on preserving old film, which is subject to degradation of its [Šfilm stock]º. In spite of its name, AFI does not focus exclusively on [„film], but also on [Štelevision]… and […video]ˆ.

In [„1973]˜, the AFI established a [±AFI Life Achievement Award|Life Achievement Award]‰. 

In [198]‡, the 10„th an©iversary of American film, AFI began its [10 Years Series]Ó, celebrating and promoting interest in film history. 

They recently opened the [ŠAFI Silver]Œ theatre in [—Silver Spring, Maryland]† near [Washington, D.C.]„

