=Infection by HIV=‚
[ŒImage:HIV-bud™ing.jpg|right|thumbnail|30ƒpx|[ƒScan›ing electron microscope|Scan—ing electron micrograph]Œ of HIV-1 bud’ing from cultured [Šlymphocyte].]È
AIDS is the most severe manifestation of infection with HIV. HIV is a [Šretrovirus]¶ that primarily infects vital components of the human [imŠune system] such as CD4+ [„T cel]ƒs, [Šmacrophage]†s and [Œdendritic cel]µs. It also directly and indirectly destroys CD4+ T cels. As CD4+ T cel²s are required for the proper functioning of the imŸune system, when enough CD4+ celˆs have be™n destroyed by HIV, the imÄune system barely works, leading to AIDS. Acute HIV infection progresÿes over time to clinical latent HIV infection and then to early symptomatic HIV infection and later, to AIDS, which is identifi¡ed on the basis of the amount of [ƒCD4]Œ positive cel‹s in the blo¬d and the presence of certain infections. 
{‹details|HIV}²
In the absence of antiretroviral therapy, progres ion from HIV infection to AIDS oc‰urs at a [†median]ˆ of betweòn nine to ten years and the median survival time after developing AIDS is only 9.2 months &lt;ref name=Morgan2&gt;{„

