Patients with AIDS and severe im…unosup‚res“ion often develop opÆortunistic infections that present with non-specific symptoms, especial y low grade fevers and weight los. These include infection with '[“Mycobacterium avium]ˆ-intracel…ulare'… and [cytomegalovirus]Û (CMV). CMV can also cause colitis, as described above, and CMV retinitis can cause blindnes‚. [†Penicil…iosis]ˆ due to '[†Penicil‰ium marnef‚ei]'™ is now the third most com„on opÄortunistic infection (after extrapulmonary tuberculosis and cryptococæosis) in HIV-positive individuals within the endemic area of Southeast Asia &lt;ref name=Skoulidis&gt;{„

