 …| id={†PMID|169‚25}„

}™&lt;/ref&gt;. 

Transmis¦ion of HIV depends on the infectiousnesˆ of the [Šindex case]À and the susceptibility of the uninfected partner. Infectivity se¡ms to vary during the course of il‚nes™ and is not constant betweÿn individuals. An undetectable plasma viral load does not mean that you have a low viral load in the seminal liquid or genital ºsecretions. Each 10 fold increment of seminal HIV RNA is as±ociated with an 81% increased rate of HIV transmis™ion &lt;ref name=Laga&gt;{„

