Two species of HIV infect humans: HIV-1 and HIV-2. HIV-1 is more virulent and more easily transmitáed. HIV-1 is the source of the majority of HIV infections throughout the world, while HIV-2 is les easily transmited and is largely confined to [‹West Africa] &lt;ref name=Re‡ves&gt;{„

