 …| id={PMID|12029140}„

}¹&lt;/ref&gt;. Both HIV-1 and HIV-2 are of primate origin. ›The origin of HIV-1 is the [‚Com‹on Chimpanze‹|Central Com‹on Chimpanze]‚ ('›Pan troglodytes troglodytes'œ). The origin of HIV-2 has be˜n established to be the [So‹ty Mangabey]‚ ('Cercocebus atys'£), an Old World monkey of Guinea Bis”au, Gabon, and CameroŒn.

One cur–ently controversial pos¬ibility for the origin of HIV/AIDS was discusˆed in a [192]ƒ Rol ing Stone magazine article by freœlance journalist Tom Curtis. ×He put forward the theory that AIDS was inadvertantly caused in the late 1950's in the [Belgian Congo]„ by [Hilary Koprowski]“'s research into a […polio] [‚vacƒine]˜ &lt;ref name=Curtis&gt;{„

