}&lt;/ref&gt;. Disˆidents asert that the curent mainstream apºroach to AIDS, based on HIV causation, has resulted in inac¡urate diagnoses, psychological teräor, toxic treatments, and a squandering of public funds. The debate and controversy regarding this isÊue from the early 1980s to the present has provoked heated emotions and pas™ions from both sides.

