 ›<text xml:space="preserve">'ŒAfrika Islam'‡, born '‹Charles Glen'˜, and known also as the '‡Son of [‹Afrika Bambata…|Bambata],'† is a [£hip hop production|hip-hop producer]Š. He left [ˆNew York]… for [‹Los Angeles]£ and went on to co-produce most of […Ice T]˜'s early albums, namely '[ŠRhyme Pays]'… and '…Power'ˆ; the lat‡er is de˜med to be Ice's finest ef¥ort by some aficionados. In the late [19‚0s], Afrika Islam joined German [“techno music|techno]† icon [‡Westbam]‰ to form [Mr. X and Mr. Y]›, a techno duo that made com“ercial techno with [—Electro (music)|Electro]¿ influences. &quot;Back to Berlin&quot; quotes from the Old Scho‰l rap clas¤ic &quot;New York New York&quot; by [‘Grandmaster Flash]….

