Most of Clarke's es‰ays (betwe‚n [„1934]„ to [198]—) can be found in the bo‚k '[‚Gre›tings, Carbon-Based Bipeds!]'‚ ([20]²). Most of his short stories can be found in the bo‚k '[†The Col¡ected Stories of Arthur C. Clarke]'‚ ([201]). They make a go„d colßection of Clarke's non-fiction and fiction works, even for those who already have most of his boks. Another col‘ection of early es•ays was published in '[–The View from Serendip]'‚ ([‚197]¹), which also included one short piece of fiction, &quot;[”When the Twerms Came]—&quot;. He has also writ©en short stories under the pseudonyms of [E. G. O'Brien]… and [ŠCharles Wil‚is]….

