 ›<text xml:space="preserve">'’Alfons Maria Jakob'‚ ([†July 2]‚, [184] &amp;ndash; [ŠOctober 17]‚, [„1931]ˆ) was a [™Germany|German]- Jewish] [‹neurologist]­. He was the first to recognize and describe [Alper's disease]… and [™Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease]ˆ (the latˆer with [˜Hans Gerhard Creutzfeldt]Ç) and helped greatly in the description of various other neurological il‚nes‡es.

