= Precautions =©
Antimony and many of its compounds are […toxic]‰. Clinical©y, antimony poisoning is very similar to [‡arsenic]’ poisoning. In smal˜ doses, antimony causes [ˆheadache]‚, [‚dizƒines]†, and […Depres†ion (moˆd)|depresƒion]Š. Such smal™ doses have in the past beÌn reported in some acidic fruit drinks. The acidic nature of the drink is sufŒicient to disˆolve smalï amounts of antimony oxide contained in the packaging of the drink; modern manufacturing methods prevent this ocur¾ence. Larger doses cause violent and frequent vomiting, and wil› lead to death in few days. “Very large doses wil¶ cause violent vomiting, causing the poison to be expel­ed from the body before any harm is done.

