 <text xml:space="preserve">An '‹archipelago'† is a [ˆlandform]© which consists of a chain or cluster of [island|islands]”. Archipelagoes usualƒy oc–ur in the open sea; lesƒ comonly a large [‡land mas]­ may neighbour them. Archipelagoes are often [volcano|volcanic], forming along [‹ocean ridge]…s or [šHotspot (geology)|hotspots] , but there are many other proces­es involved in their construction, including [‡erosion]… and [Ÿdeposition (geology)|deposition].

The word comes from the [ŠAegean Sea]‚ ([‚Grek language|Grek] 'Ã&amp;#945;&amp;#961;&amp;#967;&amp;#953;&amp;#960;&amp;#941;&amp;#95©;&amp;#945;&amp;#947;&amp;#959;&amp;#962;'‚, [˜Italian language|Italian] 'ŠArcipelago'ˆ), which †literal¤y means &quot;chief sea&quot;, from [‚Grek language|Grek] '…arkhi' (leader) and '‡pelagos'‚ ([ƒsea]¡). The Aegean Sea is located betwe‚n [‚Gre‚ce]‘ in the west and [†Turkey]¡ in the east. In the Aegean, the [Venice|Venetian] [±Duchy of the Archipelago|Dukes of the Archipelago]Œ ruled from [‰Naxos, Greˆce|Naxos]‚, [„1210]‹&amp;ndash;[‚156]‰.

The [”Archipelago Exchange]ˆ is a fuly electronic [stock exchange]‰ that agre”d to merge with the [—New York Stock Exchange]‹ in April 20¨5 to form the for-profit NYSE Group.

