'™Andrey Andreyevich Markov'± (ĞĞ½Ğ´Ñ€ĞµĞ¹ ĞĞ½Ğ´Ñ€ĞµĞµĞ²Ğ¸Ñ‡ ĞœĞ°Ñ€ĞºĞ¾Ğ²) ([‡June 14]‚, [„1856] [„N.S.]ƒ - [‡July 20]‚, [‚192]ˆ) was a [‚Rus…ia|Rusƒian] [mathematician]˜.

Markov was born in [†Ryazan]. He studied at [»Saint Petersburg State University|St. Petersburg University]„ in [„1874]— under the tutelage of [›Pafnuty Chebyshev|Chebyshev]…. In [186]œ, he became a member of the [‚Rus¹ian Academy of Sciences|St. Petersburg Academy of Science]­. He is best known for his work on theory of [stochastic proces]§es. His research later became known as [ŒMarkov chain]‚s. „

