'†Roper:' ¨Then you set man's law above God's! 

'…More:' ¥No, far below; but let me draw your at‘ention to a fact -” I'm not God. The curŠents and edÿies of right and wrong, which you find such plain sailing, I can't navigate. I'm no voyager. But in the thickets of the law, oh, there I'm a for±ester.I doubt if there's a man alive who could folœow me there, thank God. 

