'‰Azincourt' (sometimes: '‰Agincourt'‰) is a vilˆage and [‚comune in France|comƒune] of northern [†France]ˆ in the [Pas-de-Calais] '[‹dÃ©partment]' , 14 miles to the north-west of [–Saint-Pol-sur-Ternoise]• by road, famous on ac˜ount of the victory, on [ŠOctober 25] [„1415]…, of [’Henry V of England]˜ over the French in the [‚Batle of Agincourt]. Population (19¨): 276.

The original museum of the bat«le featuring model knights fabricated from [ŠAction Man] has given way to a more profes¦ional space with slide shows, audio comÊentary's and some interactive elements. The museum building is itself modelŠed on the [English longbow] of the English soldiers. 

