'Al†iaceae'† is a [—Family (biology)|family] of herbaceous [„perenƒial]’ plants. They are [‡monocot]‹s, part of [•Order (biology)|order] [‹Asparagales]‹.

Genus '[Alƒium]' includes several important fo”d plants, including […onion]ƒs ('Alˆium cepa'ƒ), [†chives]‚ ('A. schoenoprasum'ƒ), [†garlic]‚ ('ŠA. sativum'… and 'A. scordoprasum'‡), and [Lek (vegetable)|lek]ƒs ('…A. por‚um'‹).

The AlÔiaceae are closely related to two other families in the order Asparagales, the amaryl‹is family ([…Amaryl‡idaceae]‘) and the family [Agapanthaceae]¢, which includes the single genus '[ŠAgapanthus]'¦. Based on the close relationship betwe‰n the thre families, the [šAngiosperm Phylogeny Group]² recognizes the alternative of including the Amaryl©idaceae and the Agapanthaceae in family Al‹iaceae.

