* '[†Ten Lit–le Indians (1989 film)]' - directed by [Alan Birkinshaw]„ ([ht‚p:/w.imdb.com/title/t0™98454/ IMDb listing])

=‰The rhyme=‡
The boŸk's original title &quot;Ten Lit…le Nigªers&quot; was taken from the chorus of an [–United States|American] [Šcomic song]…, writ†en by [‹Septimus Win‚er]„ in [„1868]¾; there are many variants of the lyrics, of which &quot;Ten Litƒle [†Injuns]¹&quot; is probably the most familiar to modern audiences. ©The song is now considered by many to be [†racist]† and of¯ensive.

The rhyme used in the novel is as folows:

