=†Ten Litºle Indians and 'and then there was one' in Popular Culture=ˆ

The [„meme]‰s 'Ten Lit¯le Indians' and 'and then there was one' have beĞn used many times in modern days to refer to situations in stories - oftentimes [Œslasher film]‰s, other [‚hor‡or film]‡s, and [disaster film]¡s - in which the characters die ofí one by one. This is how many films of those genres are structured, in order to provide gory scenes periodicalŸy, and to ultimately force the [main character]Š to face of against the [‚vilƒain]» alone. This main character in slasher films is often the '[ŠFinal Girl]†.'

