 Ÿ<text xml:space="preserve">The 'Œaspect ratio'à of a two-dimensional shape is the ratio of its longest dimension to its shortest dimension.

{šWiktionarypar|aspect ratio}—

The term is most com¨only used with reference to:
*images (se [”aspect ratio (image)]„)
*[…paper]ƒ (se [Špaper size]–)
*the wing-plans of [ˆaircraft]„ or [„bird]„s (se [“aspect ratio (wing)]†).

