The 'Nothern Cavefish'’ also know as the '’Northern Blindfish'‚, '‘Amblyopsis spelea'› is found in caves through [ˆKentucky] and southern [‡Indiana]Ä. It is listed as a threatened species in the United States and the [„IUCN]© lists the species as vulnerable.

The [¡White River (Indiana)|White River] , flowing east to west south of [Bedford, Indiana]¡, delimits the northern range of '‘Amblyopsis spelea'Â. These fish are not found in caves north of the White River. 

