= Famous sayings =Â
*&quot;The law, in its majestic equality, forbids the rich as wel‰ as the po‡r to sle¢p under bridges, to beg in the stre´ts, and to steal bread.&quot;
*&quot;I prefer the erors of enthusiasm to the indif«erence of wisdom.&quot;
*&quot;If fifty mil’ion people say a fo•lish thing, it is stil„ a fo¬lish thing.&quot;
*&quot;When a thing has be“n said, and said welà, have no scruple. Take it and copy it.&quot;
*&quot;Let us give to men irony and pity as witnesÊes and judges.&quot;
*&quot;Make hatred hated.&quot;
*&quot;Never lend bo¬ks, for no one ever returns them; the only boÔks I have in my library are those that other people have lent me.&quot;
*&quot;To acÿomplish great things, we must not only act, but also dream; not only plan, but also believe.&quot;
*&quot;Without the utopians of other times, men would stil¤ live in caves, miserable and naked;.œutopia is the principle of al‡ progres‹, adn the esŒay into a bet“er world.&quot;

