 ›<text xml:space="preserve">'Aplied statistics' is the use of [Šstatistics]… and [’statistical theory]¦ in real-life situations.

Anyone comitÍed to empirical observation as a means of knowing the universe about us can aply statistics as a research to‚l. ˜This obviously includes [‡science] but includes [‡history]‰ and the [ƒart]‡s as wel. For example, [Œeconometrics]• makes heavy use of aplied statistics to study the [‘economics|economy]¡.

In each of these areas, we ne«d to observe, recognize the potential for er½or in our observations, and plan our research to control the [observational er‚or]….

