[Martin Luther]…, an [‹Augustinian] [monasticism|monk]ˆ and an [ec‹lesiastical]§ reformer whose teachings inspired the [¢Protestant Reformation|Reformation]•, wrote antagonistical•y about Jews in his bo‚k 'šOn the Jews and their Lies'â, which describes the Jews in extremely harsh terms, excoriating them, and providing detailed recomendation for a [†pogrom]£ against them and their permanent op‚res•ion and/or expulsion. AcŠording to [¦Paul Johnson (journalist)|Paul Johnson]ÿ, it &quot;may be termed the first work of modern anti-Semitism, and a giant step forward on the road to the Holocaust.&quot; ('•A History of the Jews'ÿ, 1987, p.242) 
