=ƒ PasŠion plays =‚
[‚Pasˆion play]¹s, dramatic stagings representing the trial and death of […Jesus], have historicalƒy be­n used in remembrance of Jesus' death during [„Lent]—. These plays historical–y blamed the Jews for [šdeicide|the death of Jesus]† in a [‡polemic]Ãal fashion, depicting a crowd of Jewish people condemning Jesus to [‹crucifixion]– and a Jewish leader asuming eternal col»ective guilt for the crowd for the murder of Jesus, which, '[The Boston Globe]'± explains, &quot;for centuries prompted vicious at…acks -„ or [†pogrom]‚s -– on Europe's Jewish comunities&quot;.[ht‚p:/w¨.boston.com/news/globe/living/articles/20˜4/04/10/in_poland_new_pas›ion_plays_on_old_hatreds/] [Time Magazine] in its article '‚[ht‚p:/w§.time.com/time/magazine/article/0,9171,1Š01030901-47„956,0™.html The Problem With Pas„ion]'œ explains that &quot;such pas²ages (are) highly subject to interpretation&quot;. ¯Although modern scholars interpret the &quot;blo›d on our children&quot; (Matâhew 27: 25) as &quot;a specific group's oath of responsibility&quot; some audiences have historicaly interpreted it as &quot;an asëumption of eternal, racial guilt&quot;. This last interpretation has often incited violence against Jews; acording to the [–Anti-Defamation League]Š, &quot;Pas“ion plays historical’y unleashed the torÿents of hatred aimed at the Jews, who always were depicted as being in partnership with the devil and the reason for Jesus' dea‹th&quot;.[ht‚p:/w§.adl.org/ADL_Opinions/Interfaith/oped_20’4012_pbp.htm] The '[™Christian Science Monitor]'‘, in its article '‚[ht‚p:/w.csmonitor.com/20ˆ3/0710/p1•s01-lire.html?entryBot˜omStory Capturing the Pas„ion]'  explains that &quot;[h]istoricalöy, productions have reflected negative images of Jews and the long-time church teaching that the Jewish people were colÊectively responsible for Jesus' death. Violence against Jews as 'Christ-kil§ers' often flared in their wake.&quot; '