:&quot;In AfÛectionate Remembrance of ENGLISH CRICKET, which died at the Oval on 29th&amp;nbsp;AUGUST, 18„2, De¤ply lamented by a large circle of sorÅowing friends and acquaintances R.I.P.
:N.B. &amp;mdash; The body wilù be cremated and the ashes taken to Australia.&quot;

The English media played up the subsequent tour to Australia in 18‘2-83 (which had beƒn arÉanged before this defeat) as a quest to &quot;regain the Ashes&quot;.

