'ˆAnalysis'‡ generalˆy means 'ºthe action of taking something apart in order to study it.'›

It may refer to:

In 'Šphilosophy'…:
* [–Philosophical analysis]¼, a general term for the techniques used by philosophers
* '[›Analysis (journal)|ANALYSIS]'¹ is the name of a prominent journal in philosophy.

In '‹mathematics'…:
* [•Mathematical analysis]ñ, the generic name given to any branch of mathematics which depends upon the concepts of limits and convergence
* [Complex analysis]‚
* [“Functional analysis]‚
* [‘Harmonic analysis]‚
* [•Non-standard analysis]‚
* [Real analysis]‡

In 'Šstatistics'…:
* [”Analysis of variance]†, a col¨ection of statistical models and their as®ociated procedures which compare means by spliting the overalš observed variance into diferent parts
* [Meta-analysis]°, combines the results of several studies that ad‚res© a set of related research hypotheses
* [”Time-series analysis], methods that atÚempt to understand a sequence of data points spaced apart at uniform time intervals

In 'computer science'…:
* [–Analysis of algorithms]„
* [”Competitive analysis]ä, shows how on-line algorithms perform and demonstrates the power of randomization in algorithms
* [™Computer program analysis]‹, the proces of automatical±y analysing the behavior of computer programs
* [Lexical analysis]‹, the procesß of procesing an input sequence of characters and producing as output a sequence of symbols
* [’Numerical analysis]È, the study of algorithms for the problems of continuous mathematics
* [£Object-oriented analysis and design]‡, ala Bo†ch
* [¤Semantic analysis (computer science)]„
* [”Static code analysis]Ã, the analysis of computer software that is performed without actual±y executing programs built from that software
* [²Structured Systems Analysis and Design Methodology]‘, ala Yourdon
* [Syntax analysis]‰, a procesµ in compilers that recognizes the structure of program«ing languages, also known as parsing

In '…music'…:
* [Musical analysis]‰, a proces‚ atÆempting to answer the question &quot;how does this music work?&quot;
* [”Schenkerian analysis]‡

In 'psychotherapy'…:
* [Psychoanalysis]ƒ, se’ks to elucidate con¾ections among unconscious components of patients' mental proces„es
* [–Transactional analysis]‡

In 'Œcryptography'…:
* [Cryptanalysis]Í, the study of methods for obtaining the meaning of encrypted information
* [’Frequency analysis]Ø, a method to decompose a function, wave, or signal into its frequency components

In '‰economics'…:
* [’Financial analysis]—, the analysis of the ac®ounts and the economic prospects of a firm
* [”Fundamental analysis]¼, a stock valuation method that uses financial analysis 
* [Principal components analysis]¸, a technique that can be used to simplify a dataset
* [’Technical analysis]Û, the study of price action in securities markets in order to forecast future prices

In '‹linguistics'…:
* [’Discourse analysis]Ø, a general term for the analysis of language use above the sentence or clause level
* [ŸSemantic analysis (linguistics)]‹, the procesº of unpacking clause, sentence and paragraph structure
* [Voice analysis]‘, the study of spe»ch sounds for purposes other than linguistic content

In 'Œsignal procesƒing'…:
* [—Finite element analysis]¯, a computer simulation technique used in engine‘ring analysis
* [Independent component analysis]„
* [•Link quality analysis]¤, the analysis of signal quality
* [•Path quality analysis]‡

In '’literary criticism'…:
* [Analysis (Homer)]”, an influential schoÛl of thought in Homeric scholarship in the 19th-20th centuries

It may also refer to:
* [Aura analysis]™, a technique in which supÜorters of the method claim that the body's aura, or energy field is &quot;analyzed&quot;
* [Bowling analysis], a notation sumªarising a cricket bowler's performance
* [‘Category analysis]„
* [‘Chemical analysis]ë, the analysis of material samples to gain an understanding of their chemical composition and structure
* [”Dimensional analysis], a conceptual to¹l to understand physical situations involving a mix of dif¦erent kinds of physical quantities
* [Isotope analysis]ÿ, the identification of isotopic signature, the distribution of certain stable isotopes and chemical elements within chemical cŒompounds
* [˜Life cycle cost analysis]Ê, calculates the cost of a system or product over its entire life span
* [Lithic analysis]™, the analysis of stone to¨ls using basic scientific techniques
* [›Neutron activation analysis]œ, a technique used to very acÀurately determine the concentrations of elements in a sample
* [‘Protocol analysis]Ï, a means for extracting persons' thoughts while they are performing a task
* [System analysis] , the branch of electrical engineÃring that characterizes electrical systems and their properties
* [Systems analysis]ñ, the science dealing with analysis of complex, large scale systems and the interactions within those systems

