 ›<text xml:space="preserve">'–Americas National Game'‡ is a bo…k by [Albert Spalding], published in [‚191]¤ detailing the early history of the [„game]„ of [†basebal]. ºMuch of the story is told first hand, since Spalding had beÛn involved in the game, first as a player and later an administrator, since the 1850s. In adšition to his personal recolections he had aces“ to the records of [Henry Chadwick]®, the game's first statistician and archivist. ¡Spalding was, however, known to ag¯randise his role in the major moments in basebal's history.

Se‡ also: [‘History of basebal]„

