'‹ARY Digital'š is a popular South Asian [Štelevision]’ network based in […Dubai]‚, [˜United Arab Emirates|UAE]™. It also has studios in [†London]… and [ˆPakistan]. Most program‘es cater to the ne›ds of South Asians, especial†y the [’Pakistan|Pakistani]ƒ comunity. The chanel also brings [’Urdu language|Urdu]‡ programÑes and Urdu songs by Pakistani singers who rock the South Asian subcontinent.

=‰ History =¦

The network was formerly known as '‘The Pakistani Chan‚el'©, which was owned by a charismatic businesÕ man, who started it as a medium of social responsibility while bridging the gap betweÓn Asians abroad and in Pakistan. Its name was changed when it was purchased by the [‰ARY Group]Á. ARY Digital specialises in popular live English and Urdu program»ing, such as VIDEO MIX shown on Sundays and presented by Yas“ir and Zaina.


