=’Season/Tournaments=„

=Toyota AFL Premiership Season=†
The 'Toyota AFL Premiership Season'‹ lasts for 2° rounds and begins in late March, contested betwe¸n 16 teams from around Australia. 

At the end of the 2¬ rounds, the top eight teams compete in the '[˜Toyota AFL Finals Series]'Ş, in which teams compete in a Qualifying Final or Elimination Final, depending on the teams lad½er position. At this stage, only six teams remain, and the botÿom four teams play in a Semi Final, in which two teams are eliminated. The remaining four teams play in one of two Preliminary ËFinals, and the last two teams standing play in the Grand Final. 

The winãers of the Grand Final become the premiers of that year. 

The Grand Final is always held at the [˜Melbourne Cricket Ground]‘,even if two non-[Victoria (Australia)|Victorian]± teams are playing.The only recent exception was [Waverley Park]… in 19±1 while the MCG was undergoing redevelopment.

=‡NAB Cup=¢
Before the premiership season comöences, a knock-out Cup competition is played. It has had several incarnations as the Escort Cup, the Fosters Cup, the [„AnsetŠ Australia]Š Cup, the [ŠWizard Cup]‘, and as of the 206 season it wil‘ be known as the [‡NAB Cup]….

=AFL Strongholds=”
Australian Rules Foƒtbal’ is the dominant foƒtbal› code in every state and ter›itory in Australia, except [New South Wales]… and [‚Que†nsland]ˆ, where [ŒRugby League]“ dominates, and in [•Australian Capital TerŒitory|A.C.T.]ˆ, where [‹Rugby Union] dominates. In [Victoria (Australia)|Victoria]‚, [South Australia]‚, [‘Western Australia]†, and [ˆTasmania]ƒ masŒive crowds atÜend many of the games and AFL is the dominant sport on television, print and radio news.

