=‚Hal– of Fame and Sensation=• 
A modern museum cal‰ed the Hal¯ of Fame and Sensation opened in Melbourne in 20®3 to celebrate the culture of the AFL and the [ŒAustralian Foƒtbalƒ Halˆ of Fame]Ÿ. The museum, a licenced spin-of— of the AFL was originalœy touted for the MCG, the Hal™ of Fame failed to get sup´ort of the Melbourne Cricket Club, so the new QV shopšing centre on Swanston Stre×t was chosen as the location next to one of the busiest AFL shops. Later controversy surŒounded the ap¶oint meant of an administration as the museum began run‹ing at a losê. Many blamed high entry prices which were subsequently reduced and the museum remains open to the public. ‚HalÉ of Fame and Sensation features various honour boards and artefacts as wel as a range of inßovative interactive displays designed to emerse fans and visitors in the experience of elite ausie rules.

