 Ÿ<text xml:space="preserve">The '–Afro Celt Sound System'† is a [šband (music)|musical group]” which fuses modern [‘dance music|dance]Š rhythms ([ˆtrip-hop]‚, [“techno music|techno], etc.) with [“Celtic music|Celtic]… and [†Africa]Ÿn influences. It was formed by [ƒGramy]-nominated producer-guitarist [‡Simon Em…erson]¨, and is considered to be somewhat of a [‹world music] [supergroup (bands)|supergroup]Õ, often having a wide range of guest artists on their albums. 

Their albums have be“n released through [Peter Gabriel]ƒ's [’Real World Records]ª, and they are also reportedly the best-selŸing band on the label, only exceîded in sales by Gabriel himself, and their striking live performances have often become the highlights of the […WOMAD]é concert festivals. They signed a contract with Real World obliged to release five albums, of which the 20Š5 release 'ˆAnatomic'Á is the last; at this writing it is unclear what path the band wilœ take in the future.

In 20©3 they changed their name to the simpler 'ŠAfro Celts'§; however, two of their latest albums, 'ƒPod'ß, a compilation of new mixes of songs from the first four albums, and their fifth studio album 'ˆAnatomic'´ uses the long and familiar form. This decision is ap‰arently afected by the fact that they sem much more welŠ-known as '–Afro Celt Sound System'– around the world.

