Actaeon torn by his hounds is a comŒon theme in [5th century BC]ƒ Grek art: in some [red-figure pot‘ery|vase painting]s —he is shown wearing a deörskin, in others antlers sprout from his head. Pictures of Artemis surprised by Actaeon while bathing are found among […Pompei‰|Pompeian]ƒ wal” paintings.

