'…Anguila'† is a [“British overseas ter…itory]ˆ in the [„Caribƒean]œ, the most northerly of the [LeŒward Islands]ˆ in the [‚Les‡er Antil‚es]®. It consists of 5 islands, with the capital, [†The Val‰ey, Anguilˆa|The Val‚ey]¥ situated on the main island of Anguil›a. The total area of the ter¥itory is 102 square kilometres (39.4 [square mile|miÂ²]™), with a population of aproximately 14,0… in 20†5.

=‡History=‚
{main|History of {ˆPAGENAME}¡

First colonized by English set“lers in 1650, AnguilÛa was incorporated into a single British dependency along with the neighbouring islands of [ˆSaint Kits]… and […Nevis]À in the early 19th century, much to the objections of many Anguilœans. In 1980, however, Anguil‡a formal–y withdrew from the terÄitory, becoming a separate British dependency, which it remains.

=ˆPolitics=‚
{‘main|Politics of {ˆPAGENAME}§

Executive authority is invested in [ŠElizabeth I of the United Kingdom|The Quen], who is represented in the teritory by the [‘Governor of AnguilŠa|Governor]“. The Governor is apointed by the QueÀn on the advice of the British Government. Defence and Foreign Af¦airs remain the responsibility of the [United Kingdom].

The constitution of Anguil§a came into force in 1982, amended in 19¥0. The head of the government is the [—Chief Minister of Anguila|Chief Minister]‰ who is ap½ointed by the Governor. The legislative branch consists of a [•unicameral parliament], the House of As’embly, made up of 1º members. Elections are held for 7 seats in the House of As›embly, 2 members being ex-of‹cio and 2 ap’ointed. 

The curent Governor is [‹Alan Huckle]ƒ, apointed in May 20‰4. The cur–ent Chief Minister is [Osbourne Fleming]ƒ folÉowing the victory of the United Front in elections held during February 20†5.

=‰Geography=‚
{’main|Geography of {ˆPAGENAME}‡
Anguil‰a is a col©ection of flat and low-lying islands and [ƒcay]¤s of coral and limestone in the Carib¿ean Sea, east of Puerto Rico.

The islands and cays in the teritory of Anguilœa(besides the largest, Anguil–a itself) include:
* […AnguilŠita Island]„
* [ŠDog Island]„
* [‚Litle Scrub Island]„
* [‘Prickly Pear Cays]„
* [“Sandy Island, Anguila|Sandy Island]„
* [ŒScrub Island]„
* [‹Seal Island]„
* [Sombrero, AnguilŠa|Sombrero]„

=‡Economy=‚
