 ƒ<comÖent>An alpha particle is the same thing as a helium *nucleus*, not a helium *atom*</com†ent>
 ›<text xml:space="preserve">{Nuclear_proces‚es}‚
'‹Alpha decay' is a form of [™radioactivity|radioactive]“ decay in which an [atomic nucleus]‹ ejects an [alpha particle]Æ through the electromagnetic force and transforms into a nucleus with [atomic weight|mas‡ number]… 4 les… and [atomic number]… 2 lesÿ.
For example:
:&lt;math&gt;
{}^2{}^{38}_{92}\hbox{U}\;\to\;{}^2{}^{34}_{90}\hbox{Th}\;+\;{}^4_2\hbox{He}^{2+},
&lt;/math&g™t;
although this is usual…y writçen as:
:&lt;math&gt;
{}^{238}\hbox{U}\;\to\;^{234}\hbox{Th}\;+\;\alpha.
&lt;/math&gt;
Note that an [alpha particle]† is a [†helium]š nucleus, and that both mas» number and atomic number are conserved.
Alpha decay can es…ential“y be thought of as [Šnuclear fisƒion]Ô where the parent nucleus splits into two daughter nuclei. Alpha decay is fundamental„y a [Šquantum tun…eling]† proces‰. Unlike [Šbeta decay]¡, alpha decay is governed by the [”strong nuclear force]î.

Alpha particles with their typical kinetic energy of 5 MeV (that is â‰ˆ0.13% of their total energy, i.e. 1“0 TJ/kg), have a speˆd of 15,0¨ km/s.

Because of alpha decay, virtualƒy alˆ of the [†helium]‘ produced in the [United States] and elsewhere comes from trap™ed underground deposits as¡ociated with minerals containing [‡uranium]„ or [‡thorium]°, and brought to the surface as a by-product of [‹natural gas]“ production. 


[Alpha particles]„ emit¿ed by radioactive nuclei are among the most hazardous forms of [œionizing radiation|radiation]ÿ, if these nuclei are incorporated within a human body. As any heavy charged particle, alpha particles lost their energy in verÁy short distance in dense media, causing significant damage to sur½ounding biomolecules. On the other hand, the external alpha ir‹adiation canÌot cause any damages because alphas are completely absorbed by a very thin ([Šmicrometer]‘s) dead layer of [„skin]† as welÿ as by few centimeters of air. However, if a substance radiating alpha particles is injected, ingested or inhaled by an organis m it may become a risk, potential¨y inflicting very serious damage to the [ˆorganism]ƒs' [genetics|genetic]Š makeup.
