 ›<text xml:space="preserve">'Extreme poverty' is the most severe state of [‡poverty]­, where people have minimal or very limited aces to basic necesities, such as [fod]‚, [ˆclothing]‚, [‡shelter]‚, [‰education]… and [‹health care]†. The [›World Bank Group|World Bank]± defines extreme poverty as living on US $1 or les£ per day, and estimates that 1.1 bilion people curÅently live under these conditions. Eradiction of extreme poverty and [†hunger]„ by [„2015]† is a [‚Milen˜ium Development Goals|Milen”ium Development Goal]Ÿ.

Extreme poverty is most com†on in [’Sub-Saharan Africa]….

