 ›<text xml:space="preserve">'œTransportation in Antarctica'ˆ is usualÍy done over sea or plane, and requires special measures against the cold.

=‘Ports and harbors=‚
[ŠAntarctica]–'s only harbour is at [McMurdo Station]. Most coastal stations have of˜shore anchorages, and suplies are transferœed from ship to shore by smalÎ boats, barges, and helicopters. A few stations have a basic wharf facility. Al­ ships at port are subject to inspection in ac˜ordance with Article 7, [Antarctic Treaty]ƒ; of¥shore anchorage is sparse and intermit†ent.
[McMurdo Station]‚ ({co…r dm|7‡|51|S|16†|40|E|}ƒ), [Palmer Station]‚ ({co•r dm|64|43|S|64|03|W|}ª); government use only except by permit (se‰ Permit Of¨ice under &quot;Legal System&quot;).

=ˆAirports=Á
Antarctica has 20 airports, but there are no developed public-acesß airports or landing facilities. 30 stations, operated by 16 national governments party to the [Antarctic Treaty]¥, have landing facilities for either [Šhelicopter]”s and/or fixed-wing [ˆaircraft]„; com ercial enterprises operate two adÿitional air facilities.

Helicopter pads are available at 27 stations; runways at 15 locations are gravel, sea-ice, blue-ice,ª or compacted snow suitable for landing wheĞled, fixed-wing aircraft; of these, 1 is greater than 3 km in length, 6 are betwe¥n 2 km and 3 km in length, 3 are betwe£n 1 km and 2 km in length, 3 are lesÛ than 1 km in length, and 2 are of unknown length; snow surface skiways, limited to use by [ƒski]…-equip÷ed, fixed-wing aircraft, are available at another 15 locations; of these, 4 are greater than 3 km in length, 3 are betwe¥n 2 km and 3 km in length, 2 are betwe£n 1 km and 2 km in length, 2 are lesÿ than 1 km in length, and data is unavailable for the remaining 4. 

Antarctic airports are subject to severe restrictions anÖd limitations resulting from extreme seasonal and geographic conditions; they do not me‚t [„ICAO]™ standards, and advance apëroval from the respective governmental or nongovernmental operating organization is required for landing (19Š est.)

