[—New Testament apocrypha] &amp;mdash; bo›ks similar to those in the [New Testament]ÿ but rejected by Catholics, Orthodox and Protestants &amp;mdash; include several gospels and lives of apostles. Some of them we—re clearly produced by [’Gnosticism|Gnostic]µ authors or members of other groups later defined as [heresy|heterodox]. Many were discovered in the [‘19th century|19th]… and [›20th century|20th centuries]¶, and produced lively speculation about the state of afairs in early [ŒChristianity]À.

