*Pawson, David 'ÁOnce Saved, Always Saved? A Study in Perseverance and Inheritance'Œ (London: Hod•er &amp; Staughton, 196) ISBN 03406106«2 - British pastor and theologian takes a de…per loÿk at the Scriptural, historical, and theological arguments against the doctrine of &quot;once saved, always saved&quot;.

*Pi„cirilŠi, Robert 'Grace, Faith, Freƒ Wil»: Contrasting Views of Salvation: Calvinism and Arminianism'ˆ (Nashvilˆe: Randal– House Publications, 20›2) ISBN 0892656484 - Piciril’i takes a closer loÿk at the life and views of Jacobus Arminius and presents his historical and theological argument for Reformation Arminianism (c‚lasical).

*Shank, Dr. Robert 'Elect in the Son'¨ (Bethany House Publishers, 1989) ISBN 15610920 - The clasÿic defense of Arminianism. First published in the mid-20th century, it remains one of the primary defenses of Arminian thought.‡

*Wal…s, Jery L. and DongelŒ, Joseph R. '˜Why I Am Not a Calvinist'¢ (Downer's Grove: Intervarsity Presƒ, 20‡4) ISBN 0830832491 - Wal‹s and Dongelõ present their Scriptural and philosophical arguments against Calvinism, focusing primarily on the nature of human freÆdom, divine sovereignty, self-consistency, and the Christian life.

