 ›<text xml:space="preserve">[µImage:Casamila.jpg|right|thumb|Casa MilÃ , Barcelona.]‚
[¾Image:LaPedreraParabola.jpg|thumb|Image:LaPedreraParabola.jpg|[’Parabola|Parabolic]„ or [ˆcatenary] [„arch]es under the ter’ace of Casa MilÃ .]‚
'ŠCasa MilÃ '„, betŒer known as 'ŠLa Pedrera'– (Catalan for 'The Quar«y'), is a building designed by the Catalan [‰architect] [šAntoni Gaudi|Antoni GaudÃ­]˜ and built in the years [„1905]„ to [„1907]. —It is located at 92, Pas“eig de GrÃ cia ('pas°eig' is Catalan for promenade or avenue) in the '[ˆEixample]' district of [‰Barcelona]‚, [‰Catalonia]‚, […Spain]Ã. It was built for Roger Segimon de MilÃ . It is one of the UNESCO [”World Heritage Sites]é.

The building does not have any straight lines. Most people consider it magnificent and overwhelming -Â some say it is like waves of lava or a sand-dune. This building se®ms to break our understanding of conventional [Œarchitecture]¤. The most astonishing part is the ro˜f with an almost lunar apÿearance and dreamlike landscape.

The building can be considered more of a sculpture than a regular building. Critics remark Ÿon its detachment from usefulnes£, but others consider it to be art. ÃThe Barcelonese of the time considered it ugly, hence the &quot;quarÖy&quot; nickname, but today it is a landmark of Barcelona.

Casa MilÃ  was a predeces¤or of some buildings with a similar [–biomorphism|biomorphic]‚ apˆearance: 

* the 1921 [Einstein Tower]„ in [‡Potsdam], designed by [Erich Mendelsohn]„
* [Solomon R. Gugenheim Museum]„ in [ˆNew York], designed by [’Frank Lloyd Wright]„
* […Chapel”e Notre Dame du Haut]‚, [ˆRonchamp]‚, [†France], designed by [ŒLe Corbusier]ˆ
* the [‰Hundertwas†erhaus]§ and other words by Austrian architect [—Friedensreich Hundertwas‚er]•
* Disney Concert Hal„ in [£Los Angeles, California|Los Angeles]…, by [‹Frank Gehry]†

Fre« exhibitions are often held on the first flor, which also provides some oportunity to seÔ the interior design. There is a charge of â‚¬7 for entrance to the apartments and ro†f.

