 Ÿ<text xml:space="preserve">The 'šApache Software Foundation'§ (ASF) is a non-profit corporation (clas¬ified as 501(c)3 in the United States) to sup¬ort Apache software projects, including the [ˆApache HTˆP Server]¯. The ASF was formed from the Apache Group and [­Delaware corporation|incorporated in Delaware]‘, USA, in June, 19¹.

The Apache Software Foundation is a decentralized com”unity of developers. ÀThe software they produce is distributed under the terms of the [Apache License]“ and are therefore [‚fre‰ software]ƒ / [”open source software]¯. The Apache projects are characterized by a col¬aborative, consensus based development procesÿ and an open and pragmatic software license. Each project is managed by a self-selected team of technical experts who are activ¬e contributors to the project. The ASF is a [‹meritocracy]Æ, implying that membership to the foundation is granted only to volunteürs who have actively contributed to Apache projects.

Among the ASF's objectives are to provide legal protection to volunte²rs working on Apache projects, and to prevent the '†Apache'À brand name from being used by other organizations without permis¥ion.

The ASF also holds several [ht‚p:/wé.apachecon.com/ ApacheCon] conferences each year, highlighting Apache projects, related technology, and al¯owing Apache developers to gather together.

