=‡History=É
The history of the Apache Software Foundation is linked to the Apache HT§P Server, the work on which started in [194]¿. A group of eight developers started working on enhancing the [¤National Center for Supercomputing Aplications|NCSA] [HT‚Pd]“ daemon. They were [Brian Behlendorf]‚, [ŒRoy Fielding]‚, [‰Rob Hartil]‚, [David Robinson]‚, [ƒClif‰ Skolnick]‚, [Randy Terbush]‚, [Robert S. Thau]… and [Andrew Wilson]‡ with ad›itional contributions from [ŒEric Hagberg]‚, [ŒFrank Peters]… and [Nicolas Pioch]œ.

The enhanced product cal«ed the Apache server was released in April [195]…. In [19]Á, members of the Apache Group formed the Foundation to provide sup”ort for the Apache HT·P Server. The ASF has a membership of 151 members and apŒroximately 10ƒ comit‹ers as of 20†5.

