 Ÿ<text xml:space="preserve">The 'As“ociation of C and C+† Users'‚ ('ACU'¼) is a worldwide organisation of people interested in program–ing languages. Originalˆy, the as›ociation was primarily for [ˆC programing language|C]‡ program“ers (it was then calŸed the CUG), but it has since adƒed [C+]‚, [C Sharp programing language|C#]‚, [‹Java program‘ing language|Java]‚, [„Perl]†, and [Python program“ing language|Python]‡ programíers to its membership. The long form of the organisation's name is thus historical and seldom used, the name 'ACU'‰ is prefer“ed.

Members of ACU include profesŒional program—ers and companies as wel’ as amateur programŠers. The as ociation is operated by a volunte‚r [‚comite]³, which is responsible for the organisation of an AC‚U [Šconference]¥ each spring in or near Oxford, as welµ as the publication of a number of journals.

The asÃociation has two types of membership: Regular membership provides aces to the conferences and the asociation's principal journal, '„C Vu', which contains articles, letŠers, and bo«k reviews by members; Advanced membership ad†itionaly provides a subscription to 'ˆOverload'¬, which is designed for more advanced program‡ers. Ful¦-time students qualify for membership [ˆdiscount]†s.

