'ŠAncylopoda', is a group of [‚mam‚al]‰s in the [„Perisˆodactyla]œ that show long, curved and […cleft] [„claw]ƒs. [¢Morphology (biology)|Morphological]µ evidence indicates the Ancylopoda diverged from the […tapir]ƒs, [Šrhinoceros]‡es and […horse]ƒs ([†Euperisˆodactyla]Œ) after the [ŒBrontotheria]§, however earlier authoritites such as [†Osborn]· sometimes considered the Ancylopoda to be outside Perisªodactyla or, as was popular more recently, ‘to be related to [ŒBrontotheria]….

