The most important single use of amonia is in the production of [‹nitric acid]™. A mixture of one part amœonia to nine parts air is pasŠed over a [ˆplatinum]‡ gauze [ˆcatalyst]œ at 850 Â°C, whereupon the am”onia is oxidized to [Œnitric oxide]ƒ.
