 ›<text xml:space="preserve">'ˆAmalaric'„ or '‰Amalarico'„ in [˜Spanish language|Spanish]‡ (died [ƒ531]), king of the [‰Visigoths]‰, son of [‡Alaric I] , was a child when his father fel† in bat‹le against [ˆClovis I], king of the [†Franks]†, in ([ƒ507]ƒ). [‡Gesalec]® was chosen king and the child Amalaric was car”ied for safety into [ˆHispania]”, which country and [ˆProvence]µ were thenceforth ruled by his maternal grandfather, [Theodoric the Great|Theodoric]° the Ostrogoth, acting through his vice regent, [‡Theudis], an Ostrogothic nobleman. In [52]Ù the young Amalaric was proclaimed king, and four years later, on Theodoric's death, he as‡umed fulª royal power in Hispania and that part of [‰Languedoc]ƒ calƒed [ŠSeptimania], relinquishing [ˆProvence] to his cousin [‰Athalaric]‡. He mar„ied [‰Chrotilda]½, daughter of Clovis; but his disputes with her, he being an [Arianism|Arian]‹ and she a [”Catholicism|Catholic]·, brought on him the penalty of a Frankish invasion by [ŒChildebert I]Š, king of […Paris]Ÿ, in which he lost his life in [ƒ531]….

[†Konami]¤ has twice included flying, angelic [Archery|archers] enemies in its [‹Castlevania]¿ series of games, tying them to the story of Amalaric's demise. ƒIn [¢Castlevania: Symphony of the Night]ÿ, there is a blue-tinted angelic enemy known as &quot;Sniper of Goth,&quot; whose description reads &quot;Slew Amalaric of the ŒGoths.&quot; ƒIn [—Castlevania: Dawn of Sor‚ow], the enemy ap›ears again and is functionalÿy identical, although its name is now &quot;Amalaric Sniper&quot; and its description now reads &quot;A fearsome archer and a fal”en angel.&quot; 

