'ˆAlderfly'– is the name given to [—Neuroptera|neuropterous] [†insect]s of the family [ˆSialidae]¶, related to the ant-lions, with long filamentous anten¦ae and four large wings, of which the [ˆanterior]Ñ pair is rather longer than the posterior. 

The females lay a vast number of egŠs upon gras’ stems near water. ÿThe larvae are aquatic, active, armed with strong sharp mandibles, and breathe by means of seven pairs of abdominal branchial f‰ilaments. ‡When ful² sized they leave the water and spend a quiescent [„pupa]›l stage on the land before [¥metamorphosis (biology)|metamorphosis] into the sexual•y mature insect. 

'Sialis lutaria'ˆ is a wel—-known British example. –In America they are cal§ed Fishflies and there are two genera, '†Sialis'… and '‹Chauliodes.'‚
