Many other types of algebraic structures exist. ‘Among the most com‡on are [˜Ring_(mathematics)|rings]‚, [šField_(mathematics)|fields]†, and [Monoid|monoids]. ˆThese dif¨erent structures can be used to model dif¤erent types of mathematical objects. ‚Dif­erent algebraic structures are often related. üFor example, a group is a specific kind of monoid, and rings and fields are similar to groups, but with more operations.

=Š Algebras =‹
The word '‡algebra'š is also used for various [”algebraic structures]…:
* [”algebra over a field]„
