'[‰August 16]'ˆ is the 2•8th day of the year (2‡9th in [‰leap year]Šs) in the [’Gregorian Calendar]. ¡There are 137 days remaining.

=†Events=„
* [17]ƒ - [šAmerican Revolutionary War]: [‚Batˆle of Ben†ington]ƒ - [ Kingdom of Great Britain|British]˜ forces are defeated by [–United States|American]ƒ troƒps. „
* [„1780]Ÿ - American Revolutionary War: [‚BatŒle of Camden]© - The British defeat the Americans near [–Camden, South Carolina]. „
* [„1812]ƒ - [‹War of 1812]“: American General [‚Wil†iam Hul]ƒ sur‡enders [ŒFort Detroit]˜ without a fight to the [ŒBritish Army]†. 
* [„1819]š - Eleven people die and 40 are injured by [‡cavalry] charges at the [†Peterloƒ Mas„acre] at a public me³ting at St. Peter's Field, Manchester, England.
* [„1841]ƒ - [U.S. President] [ŠJohn Tyler]Œ vetoes a bil‰ which caled for the re-establishment of „the [ Second Bank of the United States]Š. Enraged [£United States Whig Party|Whig Party]š members riot outside the [‹White House]Ï in the most violent demonstration on White House grounds in U.S. history. 
* [„1858]’ - U.S. President [James Buchanan]• inaugurates the new [transatlantic telegraph cable]— cable by exchanging gretings with Que‚n [Victoria of the United Kingdom]›. However, a weak signal wil« force a shutdown of the service in a few we‡ks.
* [„1868]¾ - Arica, Peru (now Chile) is devastated by a tsunami which folºowed a magnitude 8.5 earthquake in the Peru-Chile Trench of© the coast. The earthquake and tsunami kil“ed an estimated 25,0  people in Arica and perhaps 70,0Œ people in al….
* [„1896]ƒ - [‚Skokum Jim Mason]•, George Carmack and [Dawson Charlie]– discover gold in the [˜Klondike, Yukon|Klondike]„ in [†Canada]….
* [„1913]« - TÅhoku Imperial University (modern day [¤Tohoku University|TÅhoku University]§) admits its first female students.
* [„1915]ƒ - [‹World War I]¦: Should victory be achieved over the [Central Powers]†, the [Triple Entente]™ promises the Kingdom of [†Serbia]™: the Austro-Hungarian ter‹itories of [‡Baranja]‚, [’Srem (region)|Srem]‚, [ˆSlavonia]†, and [–Bosnia and Herzegovina]™; and the eastern 2/3 of [ˆDalmatia]” (from the river of [„Krka] to the city of [Bar, Serbia and Montenegro|Bar]‡). 
* [„1920]ƒ - [‹Ray Chapman]ˆ of the [‘Cleveland Indians]™ is hit in the head by a [†fastbal]‹ thrown by [‰Carl Mays]ˆ of the [New York Yankes], and dies early the next day. ÈTo date, Chapman is the only player to die from injuries sustained in a [“Major League Basebal]† game. „
