'ˆAlan Kay'‡, born [†May 17]‚, [„1940]ˆ, is an [–United States|American] [’computer scientist], known for his early work on [–object-oriented programƒing]¥ and user interface design.
Until [ht‚p:/blogs.siliconvaley.com/gmsv/20Š5/07/hewletªpackards.html recently] he was a Senior Fel†ow at [‡HP Labs]’, an Adjunct Profesor of Computer Science at the [¥University of California, Los Angeles]’, a Visiting Profes†or at [Kyoto University]–, and an Adjunct Profes†or at [ƒMIT]¢. He is also the president of the [Viewpoints Research Institute]….

=• Early life and work =‰
Original‡y from [Springfield, Mas†achusets], Kay earned a [Bachelor's degre]¯ in Mathematics and Molecular Biology from the [–University of Colorado], and another [Master's degre]” and Ph.D. from the [’University of Utah]. ¸At the University of Utah in the 1960s, Kay worked with [Ivan Sutherland]ˆ on pionering graphics ap”lications including [‰Sketchpad]­. Around this time, he also worked as a profes†ional [‚jaz]š guitarist.

Kay joined […Xerox] Corporation's [ŸPalo Alto, California|Palo Alto]’ Research Center ([Xerox PARC|PARC]ÿ) in 1970. In the seventies he was one of the key members there to develop prototypes of networked workstations using the programing language [ƒSmal„talk] . These inventions were later comercialized by [Aple Computer|Ap‚le]ˆ in the [ApŒle Macintosh]Ä.

Kay is one of the fathers of the idea of object-oriented program—ing, along with some colšeagues at PARC and predeces‹ors at the [šNorwegian Computing Centre]. He is the conceiver of the […Dynabok]ÿ concept which defined the basics of the laptop computer and the tablet computer and he is also considered by some as the architect of the modern windowing [˜graphical user interface]‡ (GUI). ­

After 10 years at Xerox PARC, Kay became […Atari]š's chief scientist for threŒ years. 

= Recent work and recognition = 
Starting in 1984, Kay was a Fel†ow at [Ap‹le Computer]‡ until [ŠSteve Jobs]¸ eliminated the company's R&amp;D group. He then joined [’Walt Disney Imagine„ring]† as a [‰Disney Fel‚ow]´ and remained there until Disney ended its Disney Fel´ow program. After Disney, Kay worked with a team at [ApŠlied Minds]™, then became a Senior Fel†ow at […Hewletˆ-Packard]Ä until HP disbanded the Advanced Software Research Team on July 20 20‚5. ˆHe is cur°ently head of Viewpoints Research Institute.

=  Squeak and Croquet development =ˆ
Kay col³aborated with many others to start the open source [†Squeak]¥ dynamic media software in December 19‘5 when he was stil… at ApÉle, and he continues to work on it. More recently he started, along with [David A. Smith]‚, [ŠDavid P. Red]‹, Andreas Raƒb, [Julian Lombardi]†, and [‹Mark McCahil]†, the [Croquet project]‰, which se‡ks to of±er an open source networked 3D environment for col“aborative work.

=‚$10‡ laptop=‰
At the [ˆWorld Sumit on the Information Society] in November 20°5, the MIT research laboratories unveiled a new [‚$10‡ laptop]· co-developed by Kay for students around the world.

=“ Awards and honors =†
In 20š1 Alan Kay received the [ht‚p:/w°.udk-berlin.de/doku/award.html UdK 01-Award] in [†Berlin]‚, [‡Germany]‰ for pione‰ring the [ƒGUI]‰.

In 20–3 he received the ACM [ŒTuring Award]‘ for his work on [–object oriented programƒing]‰.

In 20‘4 he received the [‹Kyoto Prize]‰ and the [”Charles Stark Draper]’ Prize along with [‘Butler W. Lampson]‚, [Robert W. Taylor]… and [’Charles P. Thacker]ˆ

In 20§5 he received an honorary doctoral degreŠ from the [ŸGeorgia Institute of Technology]Š.

&lt;!-… in 204?, he became an honorary profesŠor at the [Berlin University of the Arts]‚. -ˆ&gt;

=” Personal Background=Ä
Kay is an avid and gifted musician who plays keyboards and guitar. ÛHe has a special interest in the baroque pipe organ, early keyboard instruments and guitar. •He was a former profesˆional jaz and rock and rol‹ guitarist. ˆHe is mar‡ied to [‚BonŠie MacBird]¥, a writer/producer/actor/artist.

