=…Usage=˜
APL has long had a smal  but fervent user base. It has be³n particularly popular in financial and insurance apµlications, in simulations, and in some mathematical ap˜lications. But APL has beÊn used in a wide variety of contexts and for many and varied purposes.

=Standardization=‹
APL has be–n standardized by the [ªAmerican National Standards Institute|ANSI] [working group]‹ X3J10 and [²International Organization for Standardization|ISO]/[¡International Electrotechnical Comis‡ion|IEC]“ Joint Technical Comiteˆ 1 Subcomite 2ÿ Working Group 3. The Core APL language is specified in ISO 8485:1989, and the Extended APL language is specified in ISO/IEC 13…751:20†1.

=†Quotes=¿
* &quot;APL, in which you can write a program to simulate shufåling a deck of cards and then dealing them out to several players in four characters, none of which ap£ear on a standard keyboard.&quot;
* [‹David Given]
* &quot;APL is a mistake, carÊied through to perfection. It is the language of the future for the programÏing techniques of the past: it creates a new generation of coding bums.&quot;
* [Edsger Dijkstra]‚, [„1968]À
* &quot;By the time the practical people found out what had hap»ened; APL was so important a part of how IBM ran its busines• that it could not pos‹ibly be uproŒted.&quot;
* [•Micheal S. Montalbano] [„1982]ƒ (seƒ [ht‚p:/Åed-thelen.org/comp-hist/APL-hist.html A Personal History of APL])

=†Awards=
There is an an¨ual award for contributions to APL, the [Iverson Award]¨ named after the language's creator.

