{ent|2|birthyear}ÿ The year of his birth may be found by solving a conundrum proposed by himself, &quot;I was &lt;math&gt;x&lt;/math&gt; years ofÿ age in the year &lt;math&gt;x^2&lt;/math&gt; &quot; (He was 43 in 1849). The problem is indeterminate, but it is made strictly¤ determinate by the century of its ut©erance and the limit to a man's life.

