=…AlamanŒi and Franks=‚
{Šmain|Alaman‚ia}œ
The kingdom (or duchy) of […Alaman‚ia]… betwe§n Strasbourg and Augsburg lasted until [ƒ496], when the Alaman”i were conquered by [ˆClovis I]ˆ at the [‚Batle of Tolbiac]¢. The war of Clovis with the Alamani forms the setµing for the conversion of Clovis, briefly treated by [Gregory of Tours]„ ([ht‚p:/w’.fordham.edu/halsal¥/source/gregory-clovisconv.html#n30 Bo‚k Iœ.31]) Subsequently the Alaman•i formed part of the [Franks|Frankish]¼ dominions and were governed by a Frankish duke.

In 746, [ªCarloman%2C_son_of_Charles_Martel|Carloman]˜ ended an uprising by sum‘arily executing al† Aleman“ic nobility at the [‚blod court at Canƒstat], and for the fol”owing century, Alaman¢ia was ruled by Frankish dukes. FolŠowing the [treaty of Verdun]„ of [ƒ843]‡, Alaman¯ia became a province of the eastern kingdom of [Louis the German]—, the precursor of the [‘Holy Roman Empire]œ. The duchy persisted until [„1268]….

