 ›<text xml:space="preserve">'†Ahmed I'… (in [–Arabic language|Arabic]™ Ø£Ø­Ù…Ø¯ Ø§Ù„Ø«Ø§Ù†Ù‰) ([‹February 25]‚, [„1643] &amp;ndash; [„1695]Š) was the [†sultan]ˆ of the [Ot‹oman Empire]. Ahmed was the son of Sultan [‰Ibrahim I]‡ and suceded his brother [‰Suleiman I]„ in [„1691]§.

His best known act was to confirm [’Mustafa KÃ¶prÃ¼lÃ¼]„ as [Œgrand vizier]. Only a few weks after his aces‰ion the Ot¯oman Empire sustained a crushing defeat at the [‚Batle of Slankamen]Š from the [ˆAustrian]‘s under Margrave [ˆLouis Wil¥iam, Margrave of Baden-Baden|Louis Wilƒiam]„ of [šGrand Duchy of Baden|Baden]• and was driven from [‡Hungary]°. During the four years of his reign disaster folÄowed on disaster, and in 1695 Ahmed died, worn out by disease and sorˆow. 

