|langs='[’Ainu language|Ainu]'¶ is the traditional language, but today somewhere betwe¯n 1% and 5% of Ainu can speak it fluently, betwe‘n 5% and 10% are [‚pasŒive speakers]„ or [partial speakers]¬, and about 50% of Ainu have a very basic com›and of the language
|rels=[‡Animism]š, some are members of the [‚Rus“ian Orthodox Church]¼
|related= Modern genetics has proven they are East Asians. They are usual—y grouped with the non-[†Tungus]ic peoples of [ˆSakhalin]†, the [„Amur]‰ river valŒey, and the [“Kamchatka peninsula]„:
*[†Nivkhs]ƒ
*[ˆItelmens]ƒ
*[ˆChukchis]ƒ
