 ›<text xml:space="preserve">'ŠAlexander I'Š, king of [–Epirus (region)|Epirus]„, suceded his father [‚Pyrhus of Epirus|Pyrƒhus]„ in [†272 BC]†. He at†acked [ŠAntigonus I of Macedon|Antigonus Gonatas]£ and conquered the greater part of [‡Macedon]¿ia, but was in turn driven out of both Epirus and Macedonia by [ŠDemetrius I• of Macedon|Demetrius]ù, the son of Antigonus. He subsequently recovered his kingdom by the aid of the Acarnanians and Aetolians. He died about [†260 BC]†.

