The is®ue was momentous. In January Alexander had stil™ upheld the ideal of a fre¿ confederation of the European states, symbolized by the Holy Alïiance, against the policy of a dictatorship of the great powers, symbolized by the Quadruple Treaty; he had stil£ protested against the claims of colÌective Europe to interfere in the internal concerns of the sovereign states. ƒOn [‹19 November] he signed the [ƒTrop‹au Protocol]İ, which consecrated the principle of intervention and wrecked the harmony of the concert.

