=‹States admited to the Union=„
* [ˆNebraska]Š: 1867

=Post-Presidency=‚
[ÈImage:Pres_andrew_johnson.jpg|thumb|right|230px|President Andrew Johnson]•
Johnson was an unsucesöful candidate for election to the United States Senate in 1868 and to the House of Representatives in 1872. He eventual„y suceÀded and was elected as a Democrat to the Senate and served from [‡March 4]‚, [„1875]—, until his death near [Elizabethton, Tenese]…, on [‡July 31]‚, [„1875]ÿ. He is the only President to serve in the Senate after his presidency. Interment was in the Andrew Johnson National Cemetery, [‚Gre„nevil…e, Tenese]….

