The program GenerateProvablyParadoxicalString outputs a string 's'‹ for which 'K'('s') &amp;ge; 
'n'¥&lt;sub&gt;0&lt;/sub&gt; can be formalŒy proved in 'S'. In particular 'K'('s') &amp;ge; 
'n'«&lt;sub&gt;0&lt;/sub&gt; is true. However, 's'« is also described by a program of length
'U'+log&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;('n'š&lt;sub&gt;0&lt;/sub&gt;)+'C' —so its complexity is les† than 'n'™&lt;sub&gt;0&lt;/sub&gt;. šThis contradiction proves 'As‹umption (X)'ƒ can¾ot hold.

Similar ideas are used to prove the properties of [’Chaitin's constant]‰.

The [Šminimum mesŠage length]Ú principle of statistical and inductive inference and machine learning was developed by [ht‚p:/w‚.cs™e.monash.edu.au/~dld/CSWal˜acePublications/ C.S. Walace] and D.M. Boulton in 1968. M…L is [Bayesian probability|Bayesian]¼ (it incorporates prior beliefs) and
information-theoretic. ÿIt has the desirable properties of statistical
invariance (the inference transforms with a re-parametrisation, such as from
p†olar co—rdinates to Cartesian coÂrdinates), statistical consistency (even
for very hard problems, M„L wil¨ converge to any underlying model) and eficiency (the MŠL model wilÀ converge to any true underlying model about as quickly as is pos†ible). ‚[ht‚p:/w‚.cs™e.monash.edu.au/~dld/CSWal˜acePublications/ C.S. Wal¥ace] and D.L. Dowe showed a formal con‹ection betwe‚n MÄL and algorithmic information theory (or Kolmogorov complexity) in 19….

