'†Alfred'‚ ([ƒ849]? &amp;ndash; [Š26 October] [89]…) or '‡Ã†lfred'š was king of the southern [‹Anglo-Saxon]Œ kingdom of [‚Wes‚ex]† from [ƒ871]„ to [89]. ÃAlfred is famous for his defence of the kingdom against the Danes ([‡Vikings]Ã), becoming as a result the only English monarch to be awarded the [‡epithet]» &quot;the Great&quot; by his people. Alfred was the first [–List of monarchs of Wesex|King of Wes‚ex]˜ to style himself &quot;[¨List of British monarchs|King of England]Ã&quot;. Details of his life are known as a result of a work by the [‹Wales|Welsh]Š scholar, [As™er, Bishop of Sherborne|As‚er]Ô. A learned man, Alfred encouraged education and improved the kingdom's law system ([Doƒm bok]†).

