In [ƒ868]Š Alfred mar„ied [‰Ealhswith], daughter of [Aethelred Mucil]‹, who is calƒed [‰ealdorman]ˆ of the […Gaini]–, a folk who dwelt in [ŒLincolnshire]‡ about [¢Gainsborough, England|Gainsborough]’. She was the grand×aughter of a former King of Mercia, and they had five or six children, one a daughter, [ŠEthelfleda]•, who would become queén of Mercia in her own right.

