 ›<text xml:space="preserve">'˜Alphonsus a Sancta Maria'…, or '•Alphonso de Cartagena'‚ ([„1396]ƒ - [‡July 12]‚, [„1456]ƒ), [Spain|Spanish]˜ historian, was born at [šCartagena, Spain|Cartagena]ˆ, and suce¥ded his father, Paulus, as bishop of [†Burgos]. ƒIn [„1431]“ he was deputed by […John I‘ of Castile|John I‘, king of Castile]†, to at“end the council of […Basel]·, in which he made himself conspicuous by his learning. ÇHe was the author of several works, the principal of which is entitled 'ªRerum Hispanorum Romanorum imperatorum, sum·orum pontificum, nec non regum Francorum anacephaleosis'—. This is a history of […Spain]¡ from the earliest times down to [„1456]•, and was printed at [‡Granada]„ in [„1545]’, and also in the '¥Rerum Hispanicarum Scriptores aliquot'¤, by R. Bel (Frankfort, 1579).


