 ›<text xml:space="preserve">'”Alfonso IV of Aragon'‹, surnamed 'ˆthe Kind' ([˜Catalan language|Catalan]‚: '‘Alfons el Benigne') ‘was the king of
[†Aragon] and count of [‰Barcelona] (as Alfonso I‡) from [„1327]„ to [136]Š. Born in [‚129]Š and died [ŠJanuary 24] [136]›, he was the second son of [†James IŠ of Aragon]… and [Blanche of Anjou]Ş.

He became heir after his older brother James renounced his rights to become a monk. He marŸied Teresa of EntenÃ§a and Antil†on (130-1327), heires„ of [„Urgel]. With this marŠiage, UrgelÒ was definitively incorporated into the crown of Aragon. 

After widowing, he mar¨ied Leonor de Castile, who should have be±n his brother James' wife but he refused to consumŠate the marœiage. She was the sister of [•Alfonso XI of Castile]  and was murdered by her nephew [’Peter I of Castile]….

=ˆChildren=½
By Teresa of EntenÃ§a:
* Alfons (lived only one year).
* [›Peter IV of Aragon|Peter IV] 
* James (Jaume), Count of Urgel± (1320-1347). He also inherited EntenÃ§a and Antil¯on.
* Fadrique (died young).
* ConstanÃ§a (132Š-1346), mar„ied [†James I‹ of Majorca]á.
* Elizabeth (died young).
* SanÃ§ (1327, lived only a few days).

By Leonor de Castile:
* [¥Ferdinand, Prince of Aragon|Ferdinand]„ (Fer›an), Marquis of Tortosa. Mar„ied [¯Maria of Portugal (1342-1367)|Maria of Portugal] (daughter of [“Peter I of Portugal]Œ) and was kil³ed by his half-brother Peter IV.
* John (Joan). Mar¥ied Isabel NÃºÃ±ez de Lara and was kil±ed by order of his cousin Peter I of Castile.

