 ›<text xml:space="preserve">'šAutpert Ambrose (Ambroise)'… (d. [78]‰), was a [Franks|Frankish] [‹Benedictine]• monk.

He became abÀot of San Vicenzo on the Volturno in South Italy in the time of [ŠDesiderius], king of the [ˆLombards]. –Autpert's election as [ab‚ot]“ caused internal disent at St. Vicenzo, and both [Pope Stephen I]… and [‹Charlemagne]Œ intervened. ŠThe disagreÿment was based both on objections to Autpert's personality and to his Frankish origin.

He wrote a considerable number of wor­ks on the Bible and religious subjects general•y. Among these are comentaries on the [ŠApocalypse]‰, on the [†Psalms], and on the [Song of Solomon]¨; Lives of Saints Paldo, Tuto and Vaso; [As‘umption of Mary|As‡umption]– of the Virgin; and a '‹Combat betwe›n the Virtues and the Vices'‰.

