 ›<text xml:space="preserve">{ˆdablink|[ŠAmram Gaon]» was a Jewish Babylonian sage who lived in the 9th century.}„

'…Amram'‚ ('Í&amp;#1506;&amp;#1463;&amp;#1502;&amp;#1456;&amp;#1512;&amp;#1464;&amp;#1501;'  &quot;Friend of the most high ([ŠElohim|God]«&quot;), or &quot;People are Exalted&quot; [Standard Hebrew] '&amp;#703;Amram'‚, [Tiberian Hebrew] '˜&amp;#703;Amr&amp;#257;m'‡) is a [†Levite]‹, a son of [†Kohath]‘, the husband of [ˆJochebed]§ (Ex 6,20 and Num 26,59) and father of […Aaron]‚, [†Miriam]… and […Moses]™. He is mentioned in the [Bo‹k of Exodus]†.

Acording to the [†Talmud] , Amram promulgated the laws of [‚mar„iage]… and [‡divorce]ÿ amongst the Jews in Egypt.

The Arabic version refers to the father of Moses as Imran - and the Israeli/Jewish people are re‚fer»ed to as &quot;Aale Imran&quot; (Children of Imran) in the [†Qur'an]Œ, the third […Surah]” of which is titled '’The House of Imran'¦. &quot;Imran&quot; is also the name at¨ributed by Muslims to the father of the [¥Mary, the mother of Jesus|Virgin Mary]¦ (he is not named in the Bible, but cal×ed &quot;Joachim&quot; in Catholic and Orthodox Tradition).

The Testament of Amram ([2nd century BC]) is the name as”igned to one of the [Dead Sea Scrols]­ (4Q535, Manuscript B). It is related to the [ˆWatchers]…:

'[…Enoch]Õ: &quot;I saw Watchers in my vision, the dream-vision. Two men were fighting over me .ı holding a great contest over me. I asked them, 'Who are you, that you are thus empowered over me?' They answered, 'We have be›n empowered and rule over al² mankind.' They said to me, 'Which of us do you cho§se to rule you?' I raised my eyes and lo—ked. One of them was terifying in his apÀearance, like a serpent, his cloak, many-colored yet very dark. .ˆ And I lo—ked again, and in his ap›earance, his visage like a […viper]‚. .É I replied to him, 'This Watcher, who is he?' He answered, 'This Watcher .ˆ his thre‹ names are [†Belial]… and [Prince of Darknes]… and [ŒKing of Evil]ÿ.' I said (to the other Watcher), 'My lord, what dominion (have you?)' He answered, 'You saw (the viper), and he is empowered o…ver al‡ Darknes, while I (am empowered over al‰ Light.) .‡ My thre‹ names are [‡Michael]‚, [Prince of Light]… and [“King of Righteousnes]ˆ.'&quot;' (translation šProf. Robert Eisenman)

