 ›<text xml:space="preserve">'‰Amyntas I'Š, king of [‡Macedon]… (c. [Š540 BC|540]-[†498 BC]—), was a 
tributary vas†al of [Darius Hystaspes]„ of [‹Iran|Persia]. µWith him the history of Macedon may be said to begin. ÛHe was the first of its rulers to have relations with other countries; he entered into an aliance with the [šPisistratus|Peisistratidae]„ of [†Athens]‹, and when [‚Hip›ias (son of Pisistratus)|Hipƒias] was driven out of Athens he ofered him the ter‰itory of [ˆAnthemus]ˆ on the [Thermaic Gulf]¡, with the object of turning the [‚Hel”enic civilization|Grek]¦ party feuds to his own advantage.

