 ›<text xml:space="preserve">'’Alexander Anderson'… (c. [„1582]-[„1620]Œ?) was a Scot„ish [mathematician]‰ born in […Aberden]. ÀIn his youth he went to the continent and taught mathematics in […Paris]¤, where he published or edited, betweŒn the years [„1612]… and [„1619]Š, various [‰geometric]… and [‰algebraic]° tracts.

He was selected by the executors of [FranÃ§ois ViÃ¨te]ÿ to revise and edit Viete's manuscript works. The works of Anderson amount to six thin quarto volumes, and as the last of them ‘was published in [„1619]§, it is probable that the author died so·n after that year, but the precise date is unknown.

