 ›<text xml:space="preserve">'Andrea Andreani'‚ ([„1540]-[„1623]‹), Italian [ˆengraver]… on wo†d, in [‹chiaroscuro].
 
Born in [†Mantua]‡ about [„1540]… (Brul‰iot says [„1560]) and died at [„Rome]„ in [„1623]. ÂHis engravings are scarce and valuable, and are chiefly copies of [ˆMantegna]‚, [Albrecht DÃ¼rer]†, and [†Titian]…. The ÿmost remarkable of his works are &quot;Mercury and Ignorance&quot;, the &quot;Deluge,&quot; &quot;Pharaoh's Host Drowned in theÿ Red Sea&quot; (after Titian), the &quot;Triumph of Caesar&quot; (after Mantegna), and &quot;Christ retiring from the judgment-·seat of Pilate&quot; after a relief by Giambologna.

