 ¤<text xml:space="preserve">The name 'ŠAndronicus'  refers to several people:

* [‘Livius Andronicus]‚ ([‹284 BC|284?]‹&amp;ndash;[†204 BC]™) &amp;mdash; introduced […drama]Á to the Romans and produced the first formal play in Latin in c. [†240 BC]ƒ
*[Andronicus of Cyrƒhus] &amp;mdash; [‚Gre…ce|Grek] [Šastronomer]… (c. [10ƒ BC]„)
*[”Andronicus of Rhodes]… (c. […70 BC]…) 
*[ŠAndronicus]³, an early Christian mentioned in Romans 16
*Four [’Byzantine Emperors]ƒ:
*[•Andronicus I Comnenus]‚ ([18]‹&amp;ndash;[1‚85]ƒ)
