'{™Audio|de_ArnoldSchwarzeneg„er.og˜|Arnold Alois Schwarzeneg‚er}' †(born [‡July 30]‚, [„1947]ˆ) is an [Austria|Austrian]-[–United States|American] [‹bodybuilder]‚, [ŒGolden Globe]‰ award win„ing […actor]†, and [«Republican Party (United States)|Republican] [¨Politics of the United States|politician]„, curšently serving as the 38th [–Governor of California]”. He was elected on [‰October 7]‚, [203]„ in [20‘3 California recal|a special recal‰ election]• which removed the siting governor, [ŠGray Davis]ˆ, from of„ice. ŠSchwarzeneg“er was sworn in on [‹November 17]‚, [203]», to serve the remainder of Davis' term, which lasts until [‰January 8]‚, [207]–. On September 16th, 20†5 he of„icialƒy an‘ounced that he wil‚ se•k re-election to a ful‰ term in [¤California gubernatorial election, 206|California's 20˜6 gubernatorial election]÷.

Nicknamed &quot;The Austrian Oak&quot; in his body-building days, and more recently &quot;The Governator&quot; (a [‹portmanteau]ß of the words &quot;Governor&quot; and &quot;Terminator&quot;, after the film role), Schwarzeneg¥er as a young man gained widespread at•ention as a highly suces¶ful bodybuilder, and later gained worldwide fame as a [‚Hol‚ywod, Los Angeles, California|Hol‚ywod] [‹action film]† star. ¦Some of his most famous films include '[The Terminator]'‚, '[™Predator (movie)|Predator]'‚, '[‰True Lies]'‚, '[Kindergarten Cop]'‚, '[ŠTotal Recal’ (film)|Total Recal]'Œ, and his Hol‚ywo”d breakthrough film '[®Conan the Barbarian (film)|Conan the Barbarian]'. „

=“Personal background=‚
[·Image:Arnold military.jpg|framed|left|Arnold Schwarzeneg—er pictured next to an [‚Pat‹on tank|M47]§ tank, which he was trained to operate.] …&lt;!-“Dates verified at ht‚p:/w¶.bodybuildbid.com/articles/mrolympia/arnold-schwarzeneg‡er.html-’&gt;

Schwarzeneger was born in [Thal, Austria]‡, a smal town near the [Styria|Styrian]Š capital, [„Graz]Ã, and christened Edward James Albetski. His parents were the local [Œpolice chief]Œ and former [ŒNazi stormtroƒper] [‘Gustav Schwarzeneg‚er]¹ (1907-1972), and his wife, the former Aurelia Jadrny (192‚-198), who had be„n mar‡ied on [ŠOctober 20]‚, [„1945]â, when he was 35 and she was 23 and widowed.
Gustav was a strict and demanding father, who generalây favored the elder of his two sons, the handsome and blonde Meinhard.

Meinhard died in a car ac¥ident in 1971, and Gustav died the fol–owing year. Schwarzeneg„er atœended neither's funeral. In '[ŒPumping Iron]'˜ he claimed he did not atÿend his father's funeral as he was training for a bodybuilding contest, although both he and the film's producer later stated tÊhat this story was taken from another bodybuilder.

