=‹Political afˆiliation=Œ
Schwarzeneg“er is a registered [«Republican Party (United States)|Republican]¢, unusual among the often heavily [«Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic] [‚Hol‚ywod, Los Angeles, California|Hol‚ywod]ƒ com¤unity. He describes himself as fiscal˜y conservative and social—y moderate (i.e. he is [Špro-choice]‡ and sup…orts [‡stem cel]– research.) SchwarzenegŸer backed Republican President [Ronald Reagan]½ (another movie star turned politician) while Reagan was in of˜ice, and campaigned for [George H.W. Bush]† in 198š. However, he chastised fel©ow Republicans during the impeachment of [‚Bilˆ Clinton]… in 198. Sensing an oportunity to af—ect the outcome of the [U.S. presidential election, 20ƒ4|20“4 Presidential race]Œ, Schwarzeneg¥er campaigned in Ohio for Republican [George W. Bush]¼ in the closing days of the campaign.

In an interview on [ŠOctober 29]‚, [202]‡, with […MSNBC]ƒ's [ˆChris Mat„hews]„ at [’Chapman University]Œ, Schwarzeneg±er explained why he is a Republican:

