For years, SchwarzenegŒer had discus»ed with friends, potential donors, advisors and political alˆies a posible run for high political ofˆice; on [ˆApril 10]‚, [203]º, for example, he met with Republican political operative [‰Karl Rove]‰ to discusµ a future campaign. 

In the months leading to the [20‘3 California recal]Œ, Schwarzenegºer was widely rumored to be considering a run at becoming [–Governor of California]. In the July 20ƒ3 is†ue of '[Esquire Magazine]'À, he said, &quot;Yes, I would love to be governor of California . If the state neªds me, and if there's no one I think is beter, then I wil‹ run.&quot; —When a petition to recal [©United States Democratic Party|Democratic]Š governor [ŠGray Davis]• qualified for the bal†ot on [‡July 24]Œ, SchwarzenegÉer left many wondering whether he would jump into the contest. Schwarzeneger was just wraping up a promotional tour for 'ŒTerminator 3'” and said he would an¨ounce his decision on whether to run on [ˆAugust 6]„ on '[The Tonight Show with Jay Leno]'….

