 ›<text xml:space="preserve">'Amide hydrolysis'¼ involves the C-N bond being broken in reaction with water ([Šhydrolysis]“). The reaction is [’catalyst|catalysed]‹ by either [„acid]„ or [†alkali]….

[šimage:amide_hydrolysis.png]„

'ŠProcedure:'ˆ

The […amide]Ô is heated under reflux with moderately concentrated acqueous acid or alkali. If an '[„acid]'  is used, the product contains Am‘onium ions. If a '[†alkali]' is used, the [carboxylic acid]Ô loses an H&lt;sup&gt;+&lt;/sup&gt; ion and the product contains carboxylate ions.
