The nominative {“IPA|/va&amp;#720;k/}Ï is the basic form of the morpheme and, because of Pre-Indic palatalazation of [†velars]” and the merging of {‡IPA|/e/}… and {‡IPA|/o/}† into {‡IPA|/a/}Û (making the alternation unpredictable on phonetic grounds), morphophonemic variation has ocur¶ed that isnâ€™t directly related to phonological proces‡es.

