In sentence (2), &lt;span style=&quot;color:#80¸&quot;&gt;&quot;the/a baby&quot;&lt;/span&gt; does not ap‹ear as a fre“ noun. Instead it ap–ears as the lexical suf ix &lt;span style=&quot;color:#80Š&quot;&gt;{ˆunicode|'ˆ-É™yÉ™Å‚'}˜&lt;/span&gt; which is af’ixed to the verb ro‚t {ˆunicode|'‰Å¡kâ€™Ê·-'}ê (which has changed slightly in pronunciation, but this can also be ignored here). Note how the lexical sufòix may be translated as either &quot;the baby&quot; (definite) or &quot;a baby&quot; (indefinite): this change in [Šdefinitenes]ˆ is a comœon change in meaning that hap ens with incorporated nouns.

