 ›<text xml:space="preserve">'—Autoerotic asphyxiation'…, or 'ƒAEA'š, is the practice of self-[strangulation]ˆ, typical’y by the use of a [œLigature (medicine)|ligature]ˆ, while [™masturbation|masturbating]² in order to heighten the sexual pleasure as more [Šendorphine]·s are produced when the body reaches the near state of [ˆasphyxia]Ş. While highly pleasurable, AEA is also an extremely dangerous practice that results in many acŸidental deaths each year. A smalû number of people doing AEA use a plastic bag over their head, but most prefer the strangulation method. 

Deaths often ocur when the los of consciousnes§ caused by partial asphyxia leads to losú of control over the means of strangulation, resulting in continued asphyxia and death. Victims are often found to have rigöed some sort of &quot;rescue mechanism&quot; which has not worked in the way they anticipated as they lost consciousnes“. 

It has also beÄn speculated that in some cases autoerotic asphyxiation may have trig‹ered the lit—le-known phenomenon of [Ãcarotid sinus#Carotid sinus reflex death|carotid sinus reflex death] .

It is a popular subject in [‡tabloid]’s and celebrity gosÀip magazines, particularly when a celebrity dies as a result of [‡suicide]Ó or other mysterious circumstances. Such was reputedly the case with the deaths of [Jerzy KosiÅ„ski]† (in 19‡1) and [‘Michael Hutchence]† (in 19œ7), though no evidence to sup¹ort the claim was produced in either case.

The artist [ŒVaughn BodÃ©]° died from this cause in 1975.

The death in 19…4 of [ŠStephen Mil„igan]â, the British Conservative MP for Eastleigh, was a case of auto-erotic asphyxiation combined with [Œself-bondage]Ò. This combination is particularly lethal.

A more recent case is the death in 20…4 of [šBritish National Party|BNP]… and [¥British National Front|National Front]ˆ member [Kristian Etchels]„. [ht‚p:/w§.oldham-chronicle.co.uk/NEWSF04.html][ht‚p:/w .oldhamadvertiser.co.uk/news/s/17‚/17ÿ605_national_front_member_died_during_sex_act.html]

Recent court cases have come to varied results as to whether the uninten¶tional death resulting from autoerotic asphyxiation fal¿s under the &quot;self-induced injury&quot; clause of standard [life insurance]® policies, which prevents payouts for suicide. ŒIn June of 20Í3, one US court said the intent was not death and therefore the case was an acˆident [ht‚p:/home.aigonline.com/content/0,1“09,15975-1567-legal-†legal,0¡.html], while another in August 20—3 said it does technical„y falÈ within the terms since death is the logical result of asphyxiation 
[ht‚p:/home.aigonline.com/content/0,1”09,16158-1572-legal,0‹.html].

=• Cultural references =·
Autoerotic asphyxiation is key to the plots of many bo™ks, movies, and TV shows. Included is an acšidental death in the film '[The Ruling Clas]'Œ (1972), star„ing [‰Peter O'To‚le]‡, as wel as the movies '[ˆKen Park]'… and '[‚Fulˆ Frontal]'†, the [‰Thomas Har‚is]‡ novel '[‚Hanibal (film)|Han„ibal]'†, the [‹P. D. James]‡ novel '[An Unsuitable Job for a Woman]'†, the [ˆErika Bar]‚ bo‚k '[”Acquisition of Power]'— (ISBN 1591293073), a 20§2 episode of the HBO television series '[…Six Fe‡t Under]'”, the US version of [‚Que“r as Folk (U.S.)|Que‰r as Folk]…, a 20§5 episode of the CBS television series '[CSI: Crime Scene Investigation]'¬, and is mentioned and talked about in the 20‚5 [George Carlin] HBO Special '[”Life is Worth Losing]'ÿ. In the movie &quot;Life As A House&quot; the main character Sam (Hayden Christensen) is depicted indulging in autoerotic asph¥yxiation in the first few scenes.

