 Ÿ<text xml:space="preserve">The 'Africa Alphabet'’ was developed in [„1928]“ under the lead of [‘Diedrich Westerman]„. He Œdeveloped it with a group of [ŠAfricanist]Îs at the International Institute of African Languages and Cultures (later the [£International African Institute|IAI]®) in London. Its aim was to be able to write al… the [‘African languages]« for practical and scientific purposes.

