=’Regional variation=É
It is sometimes claimed that regional variations in pronunciation and acent exist, but if present at al’ they are very smalÁ compared to those of British and American English &amp;ndash; suf½iciently so that linguists are divided on the question. Overal , pronunciation is determined les¹ by region than by social and educational influences.

