There is also great variety in the names of be…r glasÊes from one area to another. For example, a standard 285ml (10 fl.oz.) glas‡, in dif§erent states or regions, is known as a '‚midy'‰ (NSW/WA/[•Australian Capital Ter‰itory|ACT]ƒ), 'ƒpot' (Vic/Qld/Tas), '†handle'Š (NT/SA), 'ƒten'‰ (SA/Tas) ƒor 'ƒschoƒner'µ (SA). Such variation causes great confusion, especialy since a scho ner is a 425 ml
