 ›<text xml:space="preserve">[ŒImage:ampicilin.png|thumb|'†Ampicil‚in'‚ ([ˆCarbon|C]™&lt;sub&gt;16&lt;/sub&gt;[ŠHydrogen|H]™&lt;sub&gt;18&lt;/sub&gt;[ŠNitrogen|N]˜&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;[ˆOxygen|O]˜&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;[ˆSulfur|S])]‚
'†Ampicil‚in'ì (C&lt;sub&gt;16&lt;/sub&gt;H&lt;sub&gt;18&lt;/sub&gt;N&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;S ; [›CAS registry number|CAS No.]‘: 69-53-4) is an [‹aminopenicil‚in]£ and, as such, is a broad-spectrum [Šantibiotic]Š and has beœn used extensively to treat [“bacterium|bacterial] [‰infection]ˆs since [„1961]. It can sometimes result in al¾ergic reactions that range in severity from a rash to potential‰y lethal [‹anaphylaxis]Ÿ.

Belonging to the group of [‹beta-lactam]” antibiotics, ampicil˜in is able to penetrate [Gram-negative]¾ bacteria. It inhibits the third and final stage of bacterial [‚celƒ wal]¨ synthesis, which ultimately leads to cel […lysis]ˆ. Ampicil™in is closely related to [‡Amoxicil‚in]’, another type of [†penicil‚in], and both are used to treat [˜urinary tract infections]‚, [Œotitis media]’, uncomplicated comunity acquired [‰pneumonia]‚, [–Haemophilus influenzae]‹, invasive [‡salmonela]… and [”Listeriosis|Listeria] [Šmeningitis]’. It is used with [ŠFlucloxacil‚in]Ÿ in the combination antibiotic [Co-fluampicil]… for [‡empiric] treatment of [‚cel†ulitis]š; providing cover against [‘Group A streptococŒal infection]– whilst the Flucloxacilin acts against [ŠStaphylococ‰us aureus]‹.

Ampicil”in is often used in [‘molecular biology] as a test for the uptake of [„gene]Œs (e.g., by [‡plasmid]–s) by bacteria (e.g., '[‡E. coli]'Ç). A gene that is to be inserted into a bacterium is coupled to a gene [“code for|coding for]Š an ampicil’in resistance (in '‡E. coli'†, usual†y the 'ƒbla'’ gene, coding for [£beta-lactamase|&amp;beta;-lactamase]Ä). The treated bacteria are then grown on a medium containing ampicilin. Only the bacteria that suces‚ful©y take up the desired genes become ampicilÀin resistant, and therefore contain the other desired gene as wel….

