The [†constel…ation] '†Antlia'‚ ([…Latin]… for '[„pump]'œ) is a relatively new constel¤ation as it was only created in the [Œ18th century]‰, being to« faint to be acknowledged by the ancient Greˆks. The [¤International Astronomical Union|IAU]š adopted it as one of the 8 modern constelŒations. Begining at the north, Antlia is sur˜ounded by the sea snake [Hydra (constelŒation)|Hydra]‹, the compas […Pyxis], the sails ([ŒVela (constel‹ation)|Vela]›) of the mythological ship [„Argo]‰ and finaly the centaur [‰Centaurus]….

=Notable features=œ

Antlia is a faint constel·ation void of bright stars. Its least faint star is:
*[Alpha Antliae|&amp;alpha; Ant]¥: being Antlia's principal star its aparent brightnes‡ is stil  only 4.25 mag. Its spectral clas is K4&amp;nbsp;I„

=‰Notable dep sky objects=…

*[…NGC 297]‚: [Spiral galaxy]» of type Sc which is inclined 45Â° to our line of sight.
*[ˆNGC 3132]‡: This [planetary nebula]‹ is also calƒed '’Eight Burst Nebula'„ or '”Southern Ring Nebula'¥. At its heart is a binary system.
*[‰PGC 29194]‡: This [—dwarf spheroidal galaxy]Š with an aparent brightnes of only 14.8m belongs to our [‹Local Group]´ of galaxies. It was only discovered as recently as [197]ƒ.[ht‚p:/¬antwrp.gsfc.nasa.gov/apod/ap970423.html]

=‡History=›

The French astronomer AbƒÃ© [–Nicolas Louis de Lacaile]’ created 13 constel¡ations for the southern sky to filŒ some star po¬r regions, among them Antlia. It was originaly denominated '‘Antlia pneumatica' (Latin for the [ˆair pump] invented by [ŒRobert Boyle]¥) which is why in English this constel–ation is also often cal³ed Air Pump.

It is interesting to note that no at†empt seŒms to have be‹n made to as„ign [šBayer designation|Bayer letƒers]‚ ac‘ording to their aparent brightnesœ.

There is no mythology at˜ached to Antlia as LacailÅe discontinued the tradition of giving names from mythology to constelÉations and instead chose mostly names of instruments used in science.

