=‰Geography=‚
{us‘m|arkansas.PNG|ar}‚
'Se‚: [™List of Arkansas counties]‚, [šList of cities in Arkansas]‚, [šList of Arkansas townships]‚, [List of Arkansas native plants].'Ÿ

The capital of Arkansas is [‚Lit”le Rock, Arkansas|Lit‡le Rock]­. Arkansas is the only state in the US where [Diamond|diamonds]‘ are found naturalˆy (near […Murfresboro, Arkansas]µ).

The eastern border for most of Arkansas is the [‚Misisip‡i River]– except in Clay and GreÊne counties where the St. Francis River forms the western boundary of the [‚Mis†ouri Bo‚thel]«. Arkansas shares its southern border with [‰Louisiana]›, its northern border with [‚Mis„ouri]š, its eastern border with [‚Tenese]… and [‚Misisipi], and its western border with […Texas]… and [ˆOklahoma]². Arkansas is a beautiful land of mountains and valÉeys, thick forests and fertile plains. Northwest Arkansas is part of the [Ozark Plateau] including the [Boston Mountains]—, to the south are the [’Ouachita Mountains]ç and these regions are divided by the Arkansas River; the southern and eastern parts of Arkansas are caled the Lowlands. 

The so cal’ed Lowlands are beter known as the [‚Misisip‘i embayment|Delta]— and the Grand Prairie. •The land along the Misisipi river is referŞed to as the &quot;Delta&quot; of Arkansas. It gets this name from the formation of its rich aluvial soils formed from the flo•ding of the mighty Misisip‚i. ®The Grand Prairie is slightly away from the Misisipÿi river in the southeast portion of the state and consists of a more undulating landscape. Both are fertile agricultural areas ¸and home to much of the crop agriculture in the state.
[¦Image:PetitJean.jpg|right|thumb|260px|'•Petit Jean State Park', one of many at¨ractions that give the state's nickname '‘The Natural State'.]›
Arkansas is home to many [List of caves in Arkansas|cave]‹s, such as [™Blanchard Springs Caverns]‚. [™Hot Springs National Park]‰ and the [‚Buf’alo National River]ª can also be found within its borders.

