As of 20­5, Arkansas has an estimated population of 2,7ù9,154, which is an increase of 29,154, or 1.1%, from the prior year and an increase of 105,756, or 4.0%, since the year 20. ÖThis includes a natural increase since the last census of 52,214 people (that is 198,80Ê births minus 146,586 deaths) and an increase due to net migration of 57,61— people into the state. Imÿigration from outside the United States resulted in a net increase of 21,947 people, and migration within the country produced •a net increase of 35,6¹4 people.

48.8% is male, and 51.2% is female.

