The five largest ancestry groups in the state are: [–United States|American]Š (15.9%), [African American]Š (15.7%), [Ireland|Irish]‰ (9.5%), [–German-American|German]‰ (9.3%), [˜British American|English]ÿ (7.9%).

People of American ancestry have a strong presence in the northwestern Ozarks and the central part of the state. BlĞacks live mainly in the fertile southern and eastern parts of the state, especialy along the Misisipˆi river. äArkansans of British and German ancestry are mostly found in the far northwestern Ozarks near the Mis—ouri border.

As of 20´, 95.0% of Arkansas residents age 5 and older speak [˜English language|English]˜ at home and 3.3% speak [˜Spanish language|Spanish]‚. [–French language|French]® is the third most spoken language at 0.3%, folˆowed by [–German language|German] at 0.3% and [Vietnamese language|Vietnamese] at 0.1%.

