But al¦ this was only a preliminary to the suces‚ atending his development of the [„iron]… and [‚stel] industries at [‚PitŠsburgh, Penˆsylvania]. £Carnegie made his fortune in the ste’l industry, control­ing the most extensive integrated iron and steÊl operations ever owned by an individual in the United States. His great inovation was in the cheap and ef‰icient mas‘ production of ste­l rails for railroad lines. 

